fn man_en_index() = "# ============================================================================\n" +
"# LUME PROGRAMMING LANGUAGE — BUILT-IN HUMAN & AI MANUAL (v1.2.0 / Wave 10)\n" +
"# Edition 2026 | Zero-C Self-Hosted Steady State | \"Lume gera Lume\"\n" +
"# ============================================================================\n\n" +
"Lume is an AI-First AND Human-Friendly systems, verification, data, and neural\n" +
"programming language. Every program can be formally proven, compiled to 27\n" +
"hardware/OS targets without a C toolchain, and inspected interactively.\n\n" +
"## QUICK USAGE\n" +
"  lume manual                    Show this manual index (English)\n" +
"  lume manual --pt               Mostrar o manual em Portugues (pt-BR)\n" +
"  lume manual <chapter>          Read a specific chapter (e.g., lume manual syntax)\n" +
"  lume manual --pt <capitulo>    Ler um capitulo em Portugues (ex: lume manual --pt sintaxe)\n" +
"  lume manual all                Read the entire 10-chapter manual\n" +
"  lume manual --json [chapter]   Emit structured JSON manual for AI/IDE tools\n" +
"  lume manual --export <file.md> Generate full Markdown manual file on disk\n" +
"  lume help <chapter>            Alias for lume manual <chapter>\n\n" +
"## FOR PROGRAMMERS AND AIs\n" +
"  lume manual ref               Factual reference: only what works today, a status per builtin and module,\n" +
"                                every example run by the test suite (start here)\n" +
"  lume manual vision            Vision and research material (chapters 1-10 mix it with the reference)\n" +
"\n" +
"## MANUAL CHAPTERS (10 CHAPTERS)\n" +
"  1. overview   (visao-geral)  Architecture (.lume vs .src), Quickstart & Workflow\n" +
"  2. syntax     (sintaxe)      Complete Grammar, fn/type/match/let & Compiler Rules\n" +
"  3. types      (tipos)        Primitives, Records, ADTs, Ownership, Decimal, Money, Tensor\n" +
"  4. contracts  (contratos)    Formal Verification (requires, ensures, law, QF_LIA, WCET)\n" +
"  5. effects    (efeitos)      Algebraic Effects (/ pure), Scoped Arenas & E-Capsules\n" +
"  6. stdlib     (biblioteca)   Standard Library & Sovereign Modules (`lume manual chameleon`)\n" +
"  7. targets    (alvos)        27 Universal Targets, MIR SSA, APK/IPA/ISO/UEFI & Silicon RTL\n" +
"  8. commands   (comandos)     Full CLI Reference across Phases 1-5 & Waves 1-10 (`lume chameleon`)\n" +
"  9. examples   (exemplos)     6 Copy-Paste Working Programs + Example 7 (`chameleon_demo.src`)\n" +
" 10. errors     (erros)        Diagnostic Error Codes ([P0002]..[W0002]) & How to Fix Them\n"

fn man_en_overview() = "# CHAPTER 1: OVERVIEW & QUICKSTART (ARCHITECTURE & WORKFLOW)\n\n" +
"## 1.1 Why Lume Exists\n" +
"Lume was designed from first principles so that both AI agents and human engineers\n" +
"can write high-assurance software with zero external C/Python scaffolding:\n" +
"- Self-Hosted Fixpoint: `lumec` (compiler), `lasm` (assembler/linker), and `lcli`\n" +
"  compile themselves to bit-identical native binaries (`stage2 == stage3`).\n" +
"- Built-in Formal Solver: Every `requires`/`ensures` contract and `law` is checked\n" +
"  at compile time by Lume's internal `QF_LIA` / `QF_ALIA` / Separation Logic prover.\n" +
"- Two Syntactic Tiers:\n" +
"  1. `.src` (Lume-Core): Canonical expression-oriented syntax compiled directly by\n" +
"     the self-hosted native compiler `lumec` and `lume_driver`.\n" +
"  2. `.lume` (Surface Lume): Indentation/block surface syntax lowered to Lume-Core.\n\n" +
"## 1.2 30-Second Human Quickstart\n" +
"1. Create `hello.src` (always use pure LF `\\n` line endings):\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn square(x: int) -> int\n" +
"     requires x >= 0\n" +
"     ensures result >= 0\n" +
"   = x * x\n\n" +
"   fn test_square() = square(9) == 81\n\n" +
"   print str(square(12))\n" +
"   ```\n" +
"2. Run directly:\n" +
"   `lume run hello.src`           -> prints `144`\n" +
"3. Run unit tests (`fn test_*()`):\n" +
"   `lume test hello.src`          -> runs all `test_*` functions\n" +
"4. Formally prove contracts:\n" +
"   `lume prove hello.src`         -> emits `QF_LIA` mathematical proof JSON\n" +
"5. Compile standalone native executable:\n" +
"   `lume build hello.src -o hello`\n"

fn man_en_syntax() = "# CHAPTER 2: SYNTAX, GRAMMAR & COMPILER INVARIANTS\n\n" +
"## 2.1 Top-Level Declarations in `.src` (Lume-Core)\n" +
"In `.src` files compiled by `lumec`, every top-level item must be one of:\n" +
"- `use <module>`               Import a module from `compiler/stage1/<module>.src` or local dir.\n" +
"- `use <module> as <alias>`    The same import; `alias.name` (or `module.name`) names `name` of that module.\n" +
"- `type Name = ...`            Algebraic Data Type (ADT) or record type definition.\n" +
"- `fn name(a, b) = expr`       Function definition (optional type annotations & contracts).\n" +
"- `pub fn name(a, b) = expr`   Public exported function.\n" +
"- `priv fn name(a, b) = expr`  Module-private function: other modules cannot call it and it never collides with their names.\n" +
"- `fn f(x: any) -> any = x`    `any` opts out of static typing: any value fits, the runtime checks its use.\n" +
"- `const NAME: T = expr`       Module-level constant (inlined into functions & contracts).\n" +
"- `law name(a: int) = expr`    Universal mathematical law proven across all inputs.\n" +
"- `print <expr>`               Top-level program entrypoint expression.\n\n" +
"## 2.1.1 Reserved Words and Names With a Special Meaning\n" +
"- Keywords (never a name): `if then else elif let in var mut match not and or own with spawn do defer errdefer`\n" +
"  `comptime quote splice scope shard fn pub use as type const law print requires ensures true false`.\n" +
"- A capitalized name is a constructor (`Nil`, `Cons`, your `type` variants), never a function or a variable.\n" +
"- Runtime builtins (`count`, `at`, `slice`, `ord`, `str`, `buf_get`, ... see `lume manual stdlib`) and the prefixes\n" +
"  `__rt_` and `__lume_` belong to the runtime: a function with such a name is refused with [R0201].\n" +
"- `ct_` at the start of a function name makes all its parameters secrets (only `secret` / `secret_*` ones when it\n" +
"  has some): an `if`, `match`, `/`, `%`, `and` / `or` or table index on them is [C0009]. Parameters named `secret` or\n" +
"  `secret_*` are secrets in any function.\n" +
"- `test_*` functions are what `lume test` runs; a `pub fn` without a `test_` of the same name gets warning P35.\n" +
"- `grad`, `value_and_grad`, `jvp`, `vjp` are the autodiff operators: a call of one of them on a function is\n" +
"  differentiated ([N0400]), so do not name your own functions after them.\n" +
"- In `ensures`: `result` is the returned value and `old(x)` the value of x at entry. `_` as a body is a hole for\n" +
"  synthesis by the intent command. `kernel_boot_entry` is the entry of a `@freestanding` kernel ([K0006]).\n" +
"- Attributes: `@export(\"C\")`, `@secret`, `@no_alloc`, `@bound(cycles: N)`, `@interrupt`, `@freestanding`, `@repr(c)`.\n" +
"- Modules: `use m as a` makes `a.name` refer to m's `name`; a name defined in two imported modules is kept apart\n" +
"  as `name__m`, and an unqualified use of it is an ambiguity error with file:line:col.\n" +
"- `use std/NAME` names the standard library's module NAME even when the project has a NAME.src (`use std/h264`).\n" +
"\n" +
"## 2.2 Expressions, Destructuring & Ergonomic Operators (10/10 DX)\n" +
"- Local binding:      `let x = 10 in let y = 20 in x + y`\n" +
"- Tuple destructure:  `let (a, b) = (10, 20) in a + b`\n" +
"- Record destructure: `let " + man_br("x, y") + " = point in x + y`\n" +
"- Pipe operator:      `x |> step1(5) |> step2`\n" +
"- Record update:      `" + man_br(" state with count: state.count + 1 ") + "`\n" +
"- Conditional:        `if a > b then a else b` or braced `if a > b " + man_br(" a ") + " else " + man_br(" b ") + "`\n" +
"- Logical (short-circuit): `a == 1 and b == 2`, `x < 0 or x > 10`, `not (a == b)` (`not` binds looser than `==`/`<`)\n" +
"- Arithmetic:         `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%`\n" +
"- Comparison:         `==`, `!=` (constant-stack `O(1)` worklist structural equality on deep lists/ADTs/records), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`\n" +
"- String concat/interp: `f\"val=" + man_br("x") + "\"`, `\"val=$" + man_br("x") + "\"`, or `\"val=" + man_br("x") + "\"`\n" +
"- `+` adds two ints or joins two strs; nothing converts implicitly: `\"total: \" + str(n)` ([T0604]); lists are\n" +
"  joined with `seq_concat(xs, ys)` (`use seq`), and `xs + [d]` is refused by `lume check` and the compiler.\n" +
"                        (raw JSON `\"{\\\"a\\\":{\\\"b\\\":1}}\"` is preserved; escape literal braces with `\"\\" + man_br("x") + "\"`,\n" +
"                        `\"" + man_br(man_br("x")) + "\"`, or `\"cost: \\$" + man_br("x") + "\"`; escapes `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\b`, `\\f`, `\\0`, `\\xHH`, `\\'`, `\\\"`, `\\\\`)\n" +
"- Record literal:     `" + man_br("id: 1, name: \"alice\"") + "` (field access: `r.id`, `r.name`)\n" +
"- List literals & ADTs: `[]` (`Nil`), `[1, 2, 3]` (`Cons(1, Cons(2, Cons(3, Nil)))`), `count([1, 2, 3]) == 3`\n" +
"- Comments:           `## Double hash starts a comment line`\n\n" +
"## 2.3 Pattern Matching (`match` — 10/10 DX)\n" +
"Lume supports `match` everywhere (top-level bodies, `let ... in`, `if`, call arguments, record fields, and `match` arms):\n" +
"1. Top-level function body `match`:\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn sum_list(xs) = match xs\n" +
"       Nil        => 0\n" +
"       Cons(h, t) => h + sum_list(t)\n" +
"   ```\n" +
"2. Nested indentation-sensitive `match` inside `let ... in`, `if`, call arguments, or `match` arms:\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn head_or_zero(xs) =\n" +
"       let y = match xs\n" +
"           Nil        => 0\n" +
"           Cons(h, _) => h\n" +
"       in y + 1\n" +
"   ```\n" +
"3. Inline braced `match expr " + man_br(" Pat => body, ... ") + "`:\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn is_empty(xs) = let res = match xs " + man_br(" Nil => 1, Cons(_, _) => 0 ") + " in res\n" +
"   ```\n\n" +
"## 2.4 Essential Technical Rules for Humans & AI\n" +
"1. Pure LF (`\\n`) Line Endings: Always save `.src` and `.lume` files with Unix LF (`\\n`),\n" +
"   never Windows CRLF (`\\r\\n`).\n" +
"2. Arbitrary Function Arity & TCO: Native SysV AMD64 codegen (`05_codegen.src`) passes\n" +
"   the first 6 parameters in `%rdi, %rsi, %rdx, %rcx, %r8, %r9` and parameters 7+ on the\n" +
"   stack with full swap-safe self-tail-call optimization (`jmp`).\n" +
"3. Fail-Closed Patterns & Bindings: Duplicate parameter/pattern/destructuring names,\n" +
"   float patterns (`1.5 =>`), and unbraced same-line nested `match` fail closed with `[P0002]`.\n" +
"4. Never edit `compiler/stage1/lumec.src` directly: edit `compiler/stage1/lume/NN_*.src`\n" +
"   and run `build/bin/lume_make amalgamate`.\n"

fn man_en_types() = "# CHAPTER 3: TYPE SYSTEM, OWNERSHIP & DATA TYPES\n\n" +
"## 3.1 Core Primitive & Composite Types\n" +
"- `int`               64-bit signed integer (`-9223372036854775808` .. `9223372036854775807`)\n" +
"- `bool`              Boolean (`true` / `false`, or `1` / `0` in untyped Lume-Core)\n" +
"- `str`               Immutable UTF-8 byte-length-cached string (`O(1)` `count(s)`)\n" +
"- `bytes`             Safe bounds-checked byte buffer (`std.bytes`)\n" +
"- `List[T]`           Linked list (`Nil` | `Cons(h, t)`)\n" +
"- `Option[T]`         `None` | `Some(v)`\n" +
"- `Result[T, E]`      `Ok(v)` | `Err(e)`\n" +
"- Record `" + man_br("f: T") + "`     Structural or nominal record (`" + man_br("x: 10, y: 20") + "`)\n" +
"- Update `" + man_br("e with f: v") + "`  A copy with some fields replaced; e is any expression (a name, a call, a\n" +
"                     field `r.b`, `(e)`); a field the record lacks is `[T2101]`, also when the record comes\n" +
"                     from a function or from both branches of an if\n" +
"- Reserved words   `if then else let in var mut match not own with spawn do defer errdefer comptime quote splice\n" +
"                     scope shard fn` cannot name a function, variable or parameter (P0002 at the declaration)\n\n" +
"## 3.2 Algebraic Data Types (ADTs)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"type Shape =\n" +
"    Circle(int)\n" +
"  | Rect(int, int)\n\n" +
"fn area(s) = match s\n" +
"    Circle(r)  => 3 * r * r\n" +
"    Rect(w, h) => w * h\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## 3.3 Financial & Tabular Types (`decimal`, `money`, `table`, `query`)\n" +
"- `decimal(p, s)`     Exact fixed-point decimal with precision `p` and scale `s`.\n" +
"                      A literal with a point (`1.5`, `0.10`) is a decimal; it prints as written\n" +
"                      (`print 0.10` gives `0.10`) and keeps exact arithmetic through parameters,\n" +
"                      lists and records (`fn avg(a, b) = (a + b) / 2.0`); an int operand is n.0;\n" +
"                      `1.20 == 1.2` is true.\n" +
"- `f64`               IEEE 754 double (builtins, no `use`): `f64(x)` from an int, a decimal, an\n" +
"                      f64 or text (`f64(\"1e-9\")`, `f64(\"inf\")`, `f64(\"nan\")`); `+ - * /` and\n" +
"                      `< > <= >=` work on it, an int or decimal operand converted; `==` compares\n" +
"                      two f64 by value. `str`/`print` give the shortest text that reads back to the\n" +
"                      same double (`0.30000000000000004`, `1.0e21`); `f64_str(x, n)` has n decimals.\n" +
"                      `f64_int` (toward zero), `f64_floor`, `f64_ceil`, `f64_round` (half away from\n" +
"                      zero), `f64_sqrt`, `f64_abs`, `f64_sin`, `f64_cos`, `f64_tan`, `f64_atan2(y, x)`,\n" +
"                      `f64_exp`, `f64_log`, `f64_log10`, `f64_pow(x, y)`, `f64_is_nan`, `f64_bits`,\n" +
"                      `f64_from_bits` (the 64 bits as an int, for binary formats). A comparison with\n" +
"                      NaN stops the program: test with `f64_is_nan`. Linux and Windows print the same\n" +
"                      digits.\n" +
"                      A parameter declared `x: f64` converts its argument with f64(x) (so `3.0` works\n" +
"                      there). `use math`: sqrt exp log log10 pow sin cos tan atan2 floor ceil round\n" +
"                      abs_f fmin fmax tofloat is_nan is_inf, f32(x) (single precision, ties to even),\n" +
"                      buf_f32_get(b, off) / buf_f32_set(b, off, x). [W0004]: an int meets an f64.\n" +
"- `money[CCY]`        Currency-parameterized monetary type (`money[BRL]`, `money[USD]`);\n" +
"                      mixing currencies (`money[BRL] + money[USD]`) is a compile-time error!\n" +
"- `table[Row]`        In-memory or WAL-persisted (`persist table`) relational table.\n" +
"- `comptime table_schema(Row)` Inspects record schema at compile time (`[D0273]`).\n\n" +
"## 3.4 Shape-Checked Tensors & Autodiff (`tensor[DType, D1, D2, ...]`)\n" +
"- Shape mismatches are caught at compile time with diagnostic `[T0300]`.\n" +
"- Supports forward/reverse automatic differentiation (`grad`, `value_and_grad`, `jvp`, `vjp`).\n\n" +
"## 3.5 Ownership, Borrowing & Hardware Capabilities\n" +
"- Linear ownership (`own T`), shared borrows (`ref T`), exclusive borrows (`mut T`)\n" +
"  verified by the borrow checker (`[O0001]`..`[O0030]`) + Perceus reuse (`__perceus_reuse_1`).\n" +
"- Freestanding hardware capabilities: `cap[Page]`, `cap[Port]`, `cap[Irq]`.\n"

fn man_en_contracts() = "# CHAPTER 4: CONTRACTS, LAWS & FORMAL VERIFICATION\n\n" +
"## 4.1 Function Preconditions & Postconditions (`requires` / `ensures`)\n" +
"Every Lume function can declare machine-checked contracts:\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"fn clamp_deposit(bal: int, delta: int) -> int\n" +
"  requires bal >= 0 and delta > 0\n" +
"  ensures result > bal and result >= 0\n" +
"= bal + delta\n" +
"```\n" +
"- If a contract can be violated, compilation fails with `[V0001]` and prints a concrete\n" +
"  counterexample assignment!\n\n" +
"## 4.2 Algebraic Laws (`law`) & Logical Implication Idiom\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"law add_commutative(a: int, b: int) = (a + b) == (b + a)\n" +
"law clamp_implication(x: int, lo: int, hi: int) =\n" +
"  if lo <= hi then clamp(x, lo, hi) >= lo else 1 == 1\n" +
"```\n" +
"- Implication Idiom (`if P then Q else 1 == 1`): Express logical implication $P \\implies Q$\n" +
"  inside `law` declarations using `if P then Q else 1 == 1`, which reduces directly to\n" +
"  decidable `QF_LIA` branches in both `lcaas.src` and the standalone proof kernel `lcert.src`.\n" +
"- Bounded products (QF_NIA by relaxation): `x * y` where `requires` bounds both factors (`dt >= 0 and dt <= 60000\n" +
"  and rate >= 0 and rate <= 10000000000`) is bound by the four McCormick inequalities, so `ensures result <=\n" +
"  600000000000` of `dt * rate / 1000` is proven by `lume prove` and certified by `lume certify`; a product with an\n" +
"  unbounded factor, or a bound that does not hold, stays unproven or refuted with a counterexample. The bound may\n" +
"  come from `requires` or from the path (`if a >= 4398046511104 then lim else a * p / 1000`), also inside a `let`;\n" +
"  bounds up to 2^62 count. A factor may be a bounded linear expression (`(255 - c) * alfa`), and a division may be by a\n" +
"  variable with a positive lower bound (`pool * p / soma`, `soma >= 1`); `lume certify` re-checks all of these.\n" +
"- Recursion: a recursive call must satisfy the function's own `requires` (proved, or refuted with a\n" +
"  counterexample); `lume certify` checks a recursive contract by induction, using the proven contracts of the\n" +
"  certificate at the calls it does not unfold, and binds it to the source (`--check-source`).\n" +
"- Booleans in proofs: a comparison used as a value (`= a + n <= 1000`, `ensures result == (a + n <= 1000)`,\n" +
"  `not f(n)`) is proved as 1 / 0. A law about a function call uses the callee's proven `ensures` when the law's\n" +
"  hypothesis implies the callee's `requires` (so a callee that calls others or multiplies bounded factors is fine).\n" +
"- Compound Termination & Proof Kernel (`lcert.src`): Verifies compound `terminates`\n" +
"  obligations (`lk_prove_term_cond` across `and`/`or` guards) and runs a built-in\n" +
"  NIST FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 Known-Answer Test (`sha256(\"abc\")`).\n\n" +
"## 4.3 Worst-Case Execution Time Bounds (`@bound(cycles: N)`)\n" +
"For real-time kernels and interrupt handlers (`@interrupt`), annotate cycle budgets:\n" +
"`@bound(cycles: 256) fn irq_timer() = ...` (violations emit `[V0002]`).\n\n" +
"## 4.4 Autonomous Verification & Self-Healing Commands\n" +
"- `lume prove <file.src>`              Prove all contracts and laws (`QF_LIA` / `QF_ALIA`).\n" +
"- `lume verify [--jobs=N] <file.src>...`  check, test, prove, fmt --check and certify many files; per-file cache by bundle hash.\n" +
"- `lume pkg publish|add|install`         package versions: store with tests, `^`/`~` requirements, lume_modules/, lume.lock.\n" +
"- `use std/hash|csv|utf8|datetime|regex|deflate|http|tls`  standard library: digests, CSV, UTF-8, dates and zones, regex, gzip, HTTP and HTTPS.\n" +
"  Builtin contracts: `buf_bits_write` is `p + n` or `-1`, `buf_get` 0..255, `buf_len` / `count` >= 0 (when the\n" +
"  result is named with `let` or returned); bound the operands of a clause in `requires` so the clause cannot overflow.\n" +
"- Official examples: `examples/topics/*.src` (run each with `lume test`) and `examples/diagnostics/` (per code, the\n" +
"  failing `.bad` program and the corrected `.fixed.src`).\n" +
"- A run-time error (exit 3) prints the call stack after its message: `  at NAME (file.src:LINE)`, innermost first.\n" +
"- `lume certify <file.src> --json`     Emit standalone cryptographic proof certificate.\n" +
"- `lume verify-cert <file.src>`        Replay proof certificate in standalone `lcert` kernel.\n" +
"- `lume heal <file.src>`               Auto-repair refuted `ensures` contracts from counterexamples.\n" +
"- `lume equiv <spec.src> <fast.src>`   Formally prove two implementations equivalent + superoptimize.\n" +
"- `lume agent cegis <file.src>`        Synthesize missing `??` hole expressions via CEGIS.\n"

fn man_en_effects() = "# CHAPTER 5: ALGEBRAIC EFFECTS, DETERMINISTIC MEMORY, ARENAS & CAPSULES\n\n" +
"## 5.1 Row-Polymorphic Algebraic Effects (`/ pure`, `/ " + man_br("io, fs, net") + "`)\n" +
"- Functions marked `/ pure` cannot perform I/O, network, process execution, or raw\n" +
"  global arena mutation; violations fail closed with `[E0200]`.\n" +
"- The effect list is optional: a function without `/ ...` has its effects inferred. A\n" +
"  function that declares a list must name every effect it performs, also through the\n" +
"  functions it calls; `[E0200]` names the missing ones (`add '/ " + man_br("net, io") + "'`).\n" +
"- Effects of the runtime builtins: `buf_*` (mutable byte buffers, changed in place) are\n" +
"  `io`, like every builtin that reads or changes state; `net_*` are `net`; `fs_*` are\n" +
"  `fs`. `use dns` functions are `" + man_br("io, net, fs, time, panic") + "`. `f64` and the\n" +
"  `f64_*` builtins are pure (no effect).\n" +
"- Custom effects are declared with `effect Name " + man_br(" fn op(...) -> T ") + "` and handled via\n" +
"  `handle expr with " + man_br(" ... ") + "`.\n\n" +
"## 5.2 Automatic Memory, Zero-Heap SRA & Scoped Arenas (`std.arena`)\n" +
"- Lume collects garbage (a mark-sweep pause proportional to the live heap) and avoids heap work\n" +
"  where it can prove it safe: Perceus reuse for provably unique values,\n" +
"  Escape Analysis & Scalar Replacement of Aggregates (`lsra_expr`: non-escaping\n" +
"  `let r = " + man_br("k1: v1, ...") + " in body` records are lowered directly into `%rbp` stack\n" +
"  slots `_sra_<r>_<k>` with 0 heap allocations), self-tail-call `jmp`, and O(1) arenas.\n" +
"- Value words: an integer of 63 bits and a string of at most 7 bytes live in one machine word and\n" +
"  never reach the heap; `int` still holds the full 64-bit range. A constructor costs 8 bytes plus its\n" +
"  fields, a record 8 bytes plus its values, and a constructor without fields is one static cell.\n" +
"- Builtins & `use arena`:\n" +
"  - `let a = arena_new(65536)`   Create a scoped region arena\n" +
"  - `mem_pack(s)` / `mem_unpack(b)`   Compress cold data (LZ4 block format, corrupt input stops)\n" +
"  - `arena_freeze(a)` / `arena_thaw(a)`   Compress an arena; a frozen page returns on first touch\n" +
"  - `arena_mark_secret(a)`, `@secret fn`   Secrets never reach the compactor ([C0009])\n" +
"  - `arena_reset(a)` / `arena_destroy(a)`\n" +
"  - `heap_stats()`               Query live heap allocations and bytes\n" +
"  - `lume run --memory <file.src>` Measure peak RSS memory in KB\n\n" +
"## 5.3 Tamper-Evident E-Capsules (`std.capsule` & `lume capsule`)\n" +
"- Seal execution traces, inputs, outputs, and SHA-256 digests into reproducible capsules:\n" +
"  - `lume capsule seal <source.src> -o <out.lcaps>`\n" +
"  - `lume capsule replay <out.lcaps>`\n"

fn man_en_stdlib() = "# CHAPTER 6: BUILTINS, STANDARD LIBRARY & SOVEREIGN MODULES\n\n" +
"## 6.1 Core Builtin Functions (Always Available in `.src`)\n" +
"- Strings:  `count(s)`, `at(s, i)`, `slice(s, start, end)`, `slicen(s, n, start, end)`,\n" +
"            `ord(ch)`, `chr(code)`, `str(n)`, `toint(s)`\n" +
"- I/O & FS: `readall()`, `fs_read_file(path)`, `fs_write_sync(path, data)`,\n" +
"            `fs_path_exists(path)`, `fs_read_byte(path, offset)`\n" +
"            `fs_read_range(path, offset, n)` (up to n bytes from offset, never the whole file; shorter at the end,\n" +
"            \"\" past it), `fs_truncate(path, size)` (1 / 0), `fs_rename_noreplace(from, to)` (0 when `to` exists;\n" +
"            renameat2 RENAME_NOREPLACE / MoveFileExW without REPLACE_EXISTING)\n" +
"            `fs_read_dir` follows a symbolic link to a folder (as opendir); on Windows `fs_chmod` with group / other\n" +
"            bits makes a private file or folder inherit its parent's ACL again (fs_mode then says 0755 / 0644)\n" +
"- Owner-only files (keys, secrets): `fs_write_private(path, data)` writes a temporary created 0600 (O_EXCL, no\n" +
"            symlink followed), fsyncs it and renames it over path: atomic, never readable by others, also on Windows\n" +
"            (a protected DACL that grants the owner alone); `fs_create_private(path, data)` creates it only when it\n" +
"            does not exist; `fs_mkdir_private(path)` makes a 0700 directory (an existing one is tightened);\n" +
"            `fs_mode(path)` gives the permission bits (384 = 0600, -1 when unreadable; Windows composes them);\n" +
"            `fs_is_private(path)` is 1 when only the owner can reach it (refuse a key file others can read, as ssh)\n" +
"- OS keychain: `use keychain` -> `keychain_set(service, account, secret)`, `keychain_get(service, account)`\n" +
"            (" + man_br("ok, value, err") + "), `keychain_delete(service, account)`: the Windows Credential Manager; on Linux an\n" +
"            owner-only file, refused on read when others can reach it; secrets up to 2560 bytes\n" +
"            `keychain_get_target(target)` reads (only) another program's generic credential by its exact target,\n" +
"            e.g. the Rust keyring crate's \"agent.omegadesk\": value (UTF-16LE text) and raw (the blob)\n" +
"            (with LUME_KEYCHAIN_DIR set it reads that directory instead; `keychain_set_target` writes there only)\n" +
"            Errors (`err`): `not_found` ONLY when the entry does not exist; `access_denied`, `unavailable` (no store,\n" +
"            no logon session, no directory), `corrupt`, `not_private`, `locked` (reserved): a store that cannot\n" +
"            answer is never reported as absent, so a caller may fail closed on it\n" +
"- Environment: `os_getenv(name)` (\"\" when absent), `os_env_has(name)` (1 when set, even to \"\")\n" +
"- Virtual interfaces (VPN): `use tun` -> `tun_open(name)` -> {{ok, fd, sess, name, err}} (Linux /dev/net/tun as\n" +
"            root; Windows Wintun in an elevated process, loaded only through the chameleon (`chameleon_c_open`): an\n" +
"            absolute path inside System32 or Program Files with a valid Authenticode signature (LUME_WINTUN_DLL, else\n" +
"            System32\\wintun.dll, then Program Files\\WireGuard\\wintun.dll); the program's folder, the current\n" +
"            folder, user folders and relative names are refused), `tun_read(t, buf)` (one IP packet: its length,\n" +
"            0 when none waits, -1), `tun_write(t, buf,\n" +
"            n)`, `tun_wait(t, ms)`, `tun_set_nonblocking(t)`, `tun_set_ipv4(t, addr, prefix)`, `tun_set_mtu(t, mtu)`,\n" +
"            `tun_set_up(t)` (\"\" or the reason), `tun_close(t)`; on Linux the fd works with epoll\n" +
"- Network control: `use netctl` -> `net_tcp_connect_addr_timeout(ip, port, ms)` (the socket, or -1 when refused,\n" +
"            unreachable or silent past ms), `net_tcp_nodelay(fd, on)` (1 when set); `use dns` ->\n" +
"            `dns_tcp_connect_timeout(host, port, ms)`. Written in Lume on the two primitives below.\n" +
"            One loop serving many clients: `net_set_nonblocking(fd, on)`, `net_send_some(fd, data)` (bytes taken,\n" +
"            0 when the buffer is full, -1 on error; no SIGPIPE), `net_recv_some(fd, max)` -> n > 0 / 0 closed /\n" +
"            -2 nothing now / -1 error, `epoll_add(ep, fd, tag, events)`, `epoll_mod`, `epoll_del(ep, fd)`,\n" +
"            `epoll_wait_ev(ep, ms)` -> tag (-1 on timeout) and events (`epoll_in()`, `epoll_out()`, err, hup)\n" +
"            Connect without blocking the loop: `net_tcp_connect_start(ip, port)` (fd at once, connect under way;\n" +
"            -1 on an immediate error), wait for `epoll_out()`, then `net_tcp_connect_result(fd)` -> 0 up, else\n" +
"            the error number (111 refused, 110 timed out)\n" +
"            Addresses: `net_local_addr(fd)`, `os_ipv4_interfaces()`, `os_ipv6_interfaces()` (short form, no ::1,\n" +
"            a link-local one with its scope: `fe80::1%3`), on Linux and on Windows\n" +
"- System primitives (for runtime and library code, effects sys / io): `sys_call(nr, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5)` is the\n" +
"            operating system call (Linux numbers, answered alike on Windows; small ints; -errno on failure);\n" +
"            `buf_addr(b)` is the address of a buffer's bytes, to build the structures a call takes\n" +
"- Process:  `os_arg_count()`, `os_arg_at(i)`,\n" +
"            `os_getpid()`, `os_exit(code)`, `os_run(cmd, args)`, `os_run_capture_timeout(cmd, args, out, err, ms)`\n" +
"            (the child leads a new process group; at the deadline the whole tree is killed: kill(-pgid) on Linux,\n" +
"            a Job Object on Windows)\n" +
"            `use process` -> `os_spawn_pipes(prog, args, new_group)` -> `" + man_br("ok, pid, out_fd, err_fd") + "` (stdout and\n" +
"            stderr as pipes; stdin /dev/null), `os_fd_read_some(fd, max)` -> `" + man_br("n, data") + "` (n > 0, 0 end,\n" +
"            -2 nothing now, -1 error; never blocks), `os_wait_nohang(pid)`, `os_wait_child(pid)`, `os_kill_tree(pid)`,\n" +
"            `os_fd_close(fd)`, `os_run_capture_limit(prog, args, max_bytes, timeout_ms)` -> `" + man_br("status, exit_code, out,") + "\n" +
"            `" + man_br("err, out_truncated, err_truncated, timed_out") + "` (at most max_bytes kept per stream, the rest\n" +
"            drained; the tree killed at the deadline)\n" +
"- System inventory: `use sysinfo` -> `fs_statvfs(path)` -> `" + man_br("ok, total_bytes, free_bytes, available_bytes, type") + "`,\n" +
"            `net_interfaces()` -> a list of records (name, mac, up, addresses: ip, prefix, family; no loopback)\n" +
"- Windows system (`use winsys`; on Linux every answer is \"absent\"): registry `reg_get_string(root, key, name)`,\n" +
"            `reg_get_dword`, `reg_key_exists(root, key)`, `reg_value_exists` (root \"HKLM\", \"HKCU\", \"HKCR\", \"HKU\");\n" +
"            sessions `wts_active_console_session()`, `wts_sessions()` (id, state, name), `wts_session_user(id)` (user,\n" +
"            domain), `process_session_id(pid)`; `services_running()` (short names of the running services)\n" +
"            services: `svc_install(name, display, description, exe, args, auto_start)`, `svc_start`, `svc_stop`,\n" +
"            `svc_remove`, `svc_state(name)`; running as one: `svc_dispatch_start(name)` -> fd of events,\n" +
"            `svc_next_event(fd)` (start, stop, shutdown, sessionchange with reason and session), `svc_set_status(state,\n" +
"            exit_code, wait_hint)`, `svc_finish()`; user session: `win_find_session_process(name, session)`,\n" +
"            `win_spawn_as_session(model_pid, cmdline, desktop)` (as SYSTEM), `win_proc_alive(h)`, `win_proc_exit_code`,\n" +
"            `win_proc_terminate(h, code)`, `win_handle_close`; named pipes: `pipe_server_create(name, sddl)`,\n" +
"            `pipe_server_accept(h, ms)` (client pid), `pipe_client_open(name, ms)`, `pipe_read_some`, `pipe_write_some`,\n" +
"            `pipe_close` (non-blocking; h works with epoll); desktops: `win_input_desktop_open()`, `win_desktop_name`,\n" +
"            `win_set_thread_desktop`, `win_desktop_close`; `win_privacy_window_create()` (black, topmost, whole virtual\n" +
"            screen, excluded from capture), `win_pump_messages()`, `win_window_destroy(hwnd)`\n" +
"            `fs_native_path(p)`: the path as Windows APIs and command lines take it (POSIX view /c/x becomes the drive\n" +
"            form with backslashes; svc_install and win_spawn_as_session apply it to the executable themselves)\n" +
"            screen, capture and input (remote desktop agents and viewers; the process becomes Per-Monitor-V2 DPI\n" +
"            aware): `win_displays()` (index, name, x, y, width, height, dpi, scale, rotation, primary, refresh,\n" +
"            monitor), `win_virtual_screen()`; `win_capture_open(index)` (Desktop Duplication through Direct3D 11,\n" +
"            GDI BitBlt when it is not available: mode \"dxgi\" / \"gdi\"), `win_capture_frame(cap, timeout_ms)` and\n" +
"            `win_capture_frame_into(cap, timeout_ms, buf)` -> status \"frame\" (BGRA data, stride, dirty rectangles),\n" +
"            \"pointer\", \"timeout\", \"lost\" (reopen: desktop switch, UAC, lock screen) or \"error\", with the pointer\n" +
"            position; `win_capture_close(cap)`, `win_capture_gdi(x, y, w, h)`; `win_cursor()` (visible, x, y, handle),\n" +
"            `win_cursor_shape(handle)` (width, height, hot_x, hot_y, color and mask BGRA, mono)\n" +
"            input: `win_send_key(scancode, extended, down)` (scancode Set 1), `win_send_vk(vk, down)`,\n" +
"            `win_send_text(s)` (Unicode), `win_send_mouse_move(x, y)` (absolute, virtual desktop),\n" +
"            `win_send_mouse_button(button, down)` (1 left .. 5 X2), `win_send_mouse_wheel(delta, horizontal)` (1/120),\n" +
"            `win_key_state(vk)` (down, toggled), `win_async_key_down(vk)`, `win_send_sas(as_user)` (Ctrl+Alt+Del)\n" +
"            viewer window (no callback: the program pumps): `win_window_open(title, w, h)`, `win_window_events(hwnd)`\n" +
"            (key_down, key_up, char, mouse_move, button_down / up, wheel, hwheel, quit), `win_window_alive`,\n" +
"            `win_window_client_size`, `win_window_set_title`, `win_window_draw(hwnd, data, w, h, stride)`,\n" +
"            `win_window_draw_rect(...)` (StretchDIBits); keyboard hook WH_KEYBOARD_LL: `win_kbhook_install()`,\n" +
"            `win_kbhook_swallow(hwnd, on)` (keep Win, Alt+Tab ... from the local system while hwnd is in front),\n" +
"            `win_kbhook_events()` (vk, scan, extended, injected, down, alt), `win_kbhook_remove(h)`\n" +
"- Byte buffers (mutable, any size): `buf_new(n)`, `buf_len(b)`, `buf_get(b, i)` (0..255), `buf_set(b, i, v)`\n" +
"            (returns b), `buf_copy(dst, d_off, src, s_off, n)`, `buf_slice(b, off, n)`, `buf_from_str(s)`,\n" +
"            `buf_to_str(b, off, n)`, `buf_addr(b)` (address of byte 0, for system calls); buf_get / buf_set on a\n" +
"            small index are inline machine code (no call), an out-of-range index stops with the same message\n" +
"            video: `buf_bgra_to_i420(src, stride, w, h, dst)` and `buf_i420_to_bgra(src, w, h, dst, stride)` (BT.601\n" +
"            limited range, 2x2 chroma average, odd sizes; the bytes written or -1 for a wrong argument; a 1080p\n" +
"            frame in a few milliseconds, runtime routines written in Lume)\n" +
"            block distortion for encoders: `buf_sad16x16`, `buf_sad8x8`, `buf_sad4x4`, `buf_satd4x4`, `buf_satd16x16`\n" +
"            (a, ai, sa, b, bi, sb): sum of absolute differences, or of the 4x4 Hadamard-transformed difference / 2,\n" +
"            between the n x n block of a at byte ai (rows sa bytes apart) and the block of b at bi; -1 when wrong\n" +
"            H.264 blocks: `buf_h264_fdct4x4` / `idct4x4(src, si, dst, di)` (int16 4x4), `buf_h264_quant4x4(src, si,\n" +
"            qp, intra, dst, di)` (nonzero levels), `buf_h264_dequant4x4(src, si, qp, dst, di)`, `buf_h264_sub4x4(a, ai,\n" +
"            sa, pred, pi, dst)`, `buf_h264_recon4x4(pred, pi, res, ri, dst, di)`, `buf_h264_intra4x4` / `intra16x16(frame,\n" +
"            fi, fs, mode, avail, dst)`; with `use h264`: `buf_h264_luma_mc(ref, ri, rs, rw, rh, x, y, mx, my, w, h, dst,\n" +
"            di, ds)` (quarter samples, 6-tap), `buf_h264_chroma_mc` (same arguments, eighth samples, bilinear),\n" +
"            `buf_h264_deblock_edge(buf, q0, across, along, lines, bs, alpha, beta, tc0, chroma)` (bs, tc0: lists, one\n" +
"            value per 4 luma / 2 chroma lines); all answer -1 on a wrong argument\n" +
"            bit writing (entropy coders, most significant bit first): `buf_bits_write(b, pos, v, n)` (the low n\n" +
"            bits of v, 1..32, at bit pos; answers pos + n), `buf_bits_read(b, pos, n)`, `buf_bits_ue(b, pos, v)` /\n" +
"            `buf_bits_se(b, pos, v)` (Exp-Golomb, answer the new pos); -1 on a wrong argument\n" +
"- Hardware & Bare-Metal Kernel Primitives (Always Available in `@freestanding` / `.kernel`):\n" +
"  - Port I/O (8/16/32-bit): `port_out8(p, v)`, `port_in8(p)`, `port_out16(p, v)`, `port_in16(p)`,\n" +
"                            `port_out32(p, v)`, `port_in32(p)`\n" +
"  - Volatile MMIO (8/16/32/64-bit): `mmio_volatile_write8(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read8(a)`,\n" +
"                                    `mmio_volatile_write16(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read16(a)`,\n" +
"                                    `mmio_volatile_write32(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read32(a)`,\n" +
"                                    `mmio_volatile_write64(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read64(a)`\n" +
"  - Native VGA Console (`0xB8000` + CRT `0x3D4`/`0x3D5`): `vga_puts(row, col, attr, text)`,\n" +
"    `vga_fill_row(row, attr, ch_ascii)`, `vga_scroll_up(top_row, bot_row, attr)`,\n" +
"    `vga_set_cursor(row, col)`\n" +
"  - CPU, MSR & SMP: `cpu_cli()`, `cpu_sti()`, `cpu_hlt()`, `cpu_pause()`, `cpu_mfence()`,\n" +
"                    `cpu_rdtsc()`, `cpu_rdmsr(msr)`, `cpu_wrmsr(msr, val)`, `cpu_read_cr3()`,\n" +
"                    `cpu_write_cr3(v)`, `cpu_invlpg(va)`, `cpu_idt_init()`, `cpu_smp_boot_ap(v)`\n" +
"  - 64-Bit Hardware Bitwise: `bit_and(a, b)`, `bit_or(a, b)`, `bit_xor(a, b)`, `bit_not(a)`,\n" +
"                             `bit_shl(a, n)`, `bit_shr(a, n)`\n" +
"  - Constant-Time Intrinsics: `ct_select(mask, a, b)` (bit by bit: `a` where the mask bit is set, else `b`),\n" +
"                              `ct_eq(a, b)` (1 when equal, else 0); both are branch-free in a constant-time kernel\n" +
"  - Block Memory, Integrity & O(1) Kernel State: `mem_copy(dst, src, len)`, `mem_set(dst, b, len)`,\n" +
"    `mem_crc64(addr, len)` (64-bit FNV-1a anti-rootkit page integrity), `krn_slot_write(idx, val)`,\n" +
"    `krn_slot_read(idx)` (zero-allocation 1024-slot kernel state table)\n" +
"- Failure:  `ctfail(msg)` (prints message to stderr and exits with non-zero code)\n\n" +
"## 6.2 Standard Library Modules (`use <module>`)\n" +
"Names across modules: a name defined at the top level of two modules is kept apart; each module\n" +
"uses its own, and the entry file keeps its names (a module's copy is renamed `name__module`, which\n" +
"is how its tests are listed). A module that uses such a name without defining it gets the one owner\n" +
"it imports (directly first); two candidates stop the build with `file:line:col` and ask for\n" +
"`module.name`. `use json as j` then `j.read(s)` names `read` of `json`, even where a local named `read` is in\n" +
"scope (the local holds only for the plain name). A module in a folder is\n" +
"written by its last segment (`use net/http`, then `http.get(u)`); of two folders with the same last\n" +
"segment, all but one need an alias (`use a/http` + `use b/http as hb`: `http.get`, `hb.get`), and two\n" +
"without one stop at `file:line:col` with that fix. Each `use m` resolves next to the file that writes\n" +
"it (`a/main.src` -> `a/m.src`, inside `d/q.src` -> `d/m.src`). Record fields are never renamed.\n" +
"- Recursion depth: the runtime reserves a large stack at start (Linux and Windows): plain recursion of a\n" +
"                       million levels runs (a list of a million items), tens of millions of small frames too; past\n" +
"                       that the program stops with `lume: stack overflow (recursion too deep)` (exit 12), never silently\n" +
"- `use seq`            Repetition without hand-written recursion: `seq_map`, `seq_filter`, `seq_fold`,\n" +
"                       `seq_foldr`, `seq_any`, `seq_all`, `seq_find`, `seq_range`, `seq_loop(a, b, acc, f)`,\n" +
"                       `seq_while(state, cond, step)`, `seq_count`, `seq_bytes`, `seq_loop_inv(a, b, acc, step, inv)`\n" +
"                       (`lume prove` proves its contract by induction on the invariant); tail-recursive, linear,\n" +
"                       a million steps in constant stack; lambdas `fn(x) => ...` may capture variables\n" +
"                       Loops: `seq_loop(0, n, acc0, fn(i, acc) => ...)` is `for i in 0..n` over an accumulator,\n" +
"                       with no list built: `fn buf_sum(b) = seq_loop(0, buf_len(b), 0, fn(i, acc) => acc + buf_get(b, i))`;\n" +
"                       `seq_loop_down(a, b, acc, f)` counts down, `seq_while(s, cond, step)` repeats while cond(s)\n" +
"- `use text`           Find by content, not by column: `str_find(s, sub, from)` (index or -1), `str_find_last`,\n" +
"                       `str_contains`, `str_after(s, label)`, `str_before`, `str_between`, `str_trim`,\n" +
"                       `str_lines` / `str_line(s, n)` (only \"\\n\" breaks a line, as sed and awk count),\n" +
"                       `str_line_with`, `str_hex_tokens(s)` (hex words, 0x dropped, `00 10` / `00:10` joined),\n" +
"                       `str_hex_after(line, \"quic key:\")` for test vectors read from RFC text\n" +
"- `use fs`             Safe file handles (`sfile_with` close-on-all-paths, `[O0001]` safety)\n" +
"- `use bytes`          Bounds-checked byte buffers (`bnew`, `bpush`, `bget`, `bslice`, `bto_str`)\n" +
"- `use vec`            Formally verified generic collection & numeric invariants (`vec.src`, `decimal.src`,\n" +
"                       `stdlib/std.lume`: `vec_clamp_index`, `vec_checked_slice_len`, `map_checked_slot`,\n" +
"                       `decimal_clamp`)\n" +
"- `use map`            Persistent hash map safe against forged collisions: `map_new()` (a secret key from the\n" +
