"\n" +
"- **`ltv` (Domain `#112`)** symbolically executes the AST and the emitted assembly of each integer function and\n" +
"  accepts only when, for every valuation of the branch atoms, both reach `ctfail` in the same cases with the same\n" +
"  message, otherwise return the same value in `%rax`, perform the same divisions / modulos / calls, and keep the\n" +
"  frame discipline (`%rsp`/`%rbp` restored, no write outside the frame). The machine model is the real one: tagged\n" +
"  63-bit integers, fast paths guarded by `jo`/`jno`, runtime helpers as stated axioms. Anything it cannot derive is\n" +
"  a rejection. Limits: integer fragment only (others are `unsupported`, never `validated`); the theorem is over the\n" +
"  integers (executions without an i64 overflow trap); the SMT-LIB2 and Lean 4 certificates in\n" +
"  `build/certification/proofs/` are checked only when `z3`/`cvc5`/`lean` are installed (`external_solver`,\n" +
"  `lean_checked` in the report say which).\n" +
"- **`lmcdc` (Domain `#114`)** lists the decisions of the lowered AST (`requires`, runtime-checked `ensures`, `if`\n" +
"  conditions, Boolean values), searches witness vectors and runs each on the real binary. An obligation without a\n" +
"  witness is reported as `theorem_false` (false outcome of a proven law or checked ensures), `infeasible` (proved\n" +
"  contradictory by the `lcert` kernel: a redundant clause or dead branch, listed for review) or `uncovered`.\n" +
"- **`lsafety_envelope` (Domain `#115`)** releases `VerifiedActuatorCommit(value)` only when channel A finished inside\n" +
"  its watchdog, channel B halted inside the cycle budget (`@bound(cycles: N)` x 16, or `--budget`) without a trap,\n" +
"  `ltv` validated the kernel, and the two words are equal. Every other case latches `SAFE_STATE_TRIP` in the\n" +
"  hash-chained log `build/certification/safety_envelope_events.jsonl` until `--reset`. Real level: channel B is a\n" +
"  software RV32IM interpreter on the same host (design diversity, not physical independence); since Wave 14\n" +
"  channel B compiles the kernel with its own clean-room front end (see the Wave 14 section below), but both\n" +
"  channels still read the same kernel text; the monitor domain is i32 (a kernel that leaves it trips).\n" +
"- **`lume qualify` (Domain `#114`)** runs 70 probes, the module batteries (ltv, lmcdc, proof status) and 16 gates,\n" +
"  checks the bidirectional traceability matrix (every requirement needs a parent, an existing source file, a passing\n" +
"  positive test, a passing negative test and a passing mutation gate or proof) and writes the dossier. It is the\n" +
"  developer's evidence package for DO-330 TQL-1 / DO-178C DAL A / IEC 61508 T3 / IEC 62304 class C work, **not a\n" +
"  qualification**: that is granted per project by the authority or assessor and needs independent verification.\n" +
"- **Soak ledger (Domain `#113`)**: `build/certification/battle_telemetry_ledger.json` accumulates the campaigns of\n" +
"  `lume soak`; each entry carries the hash of the previous one and the gate re-verifies the chain before appending.\n" +
"\n" +
"### Wave 12 Industrial Commands (Domains `#116..#121`) and the Wave 13 Closure\n" +
"  lume build --dwarf|-g <src.src> [-o <out>]             DWARF v4 line table and symbols (`.debug_line`, `.debug_info`, `.debug_abbrev`, `.symtab`, `.strtab`)\n" +
"  lume build --keep-proven-checks|--critical <src.src>   Keep the run-time check of every proven `ensures` (defence in depth)\n" +
"  lume build --target aarch64-linux-gnu|aarch64-elf|riscv64-linux-gnu|riscv64-none-elf|riscv64-none-bin|riscv32-none-elf|riscv32-none-bin <kernel.src> -o <out>\n" +
"                                                         Certified integer-kernel back ends (`larm64`, `lriscv`), `lumec` front end first\n" +
"  lume build --target safetensors [--entry <fn>] <src.src> -o <out.safetensors>   Neural cartridge of a `/ pure` integer function\n" +
"  lume proof-cache <check|store> <src.src> [<cache_dir>] [--require-all-hits]      Incremental per-function proof cache (`lproof_cache`)\n" +
"  lume verify-cert --check-source <src.src> <cert.json>  Certificate kernel with the source-to-obligation binding check\n" +
"  lume qualify --verify                                  Re-check the hash chain and the Ed25519 signature of `build/certification/`\n" +
"  lume realtime-gate | concurrency-gate | crypto-gate | multi-arch-gate | safetensors-gate | dwarf-cache-gate | cert-source-gate\n" +
"                                                         The acceptance gates of the features below\n" +
"\n" +
"- **`@no_alloc` (Domain `#116`, `[E0210]`)**: the function and every function it calls (the check is transitive)\n" +
"  must be unable to reach a heap allocation: `int`/`bool` parameters with proven bounds, `+ - *` proven inside the\n" +
"  63-bit immediate range, no record, constructor with fields, string or allocating builtin, recursion in tail\n" +
"  position only. `realtime_gate` measures the result with `heap_stats()`: zero allocations over the accepted\n" +
"  kernels. Limits: nothing is timed; `@bound` is the cycle budget. The worst-case stack depth in bytes is computed\n" +
"  separately, on the emitted code, by `lume stack` (Wave 14 section below).\n" +
"- **Constant-time kernels (`@secret` + `@no_alloc`, `[C0011]`)**: a function that carries both attributes is lowered\n" +
"  to straight-line code on immediate integers: no tag test, no overflow test, no runtime call, no jump. `[C0011]`\n" +
"  rejects everything else: parameters and result are `int`; no `requires` (mask with `bit_and`; the kernel is total\n" +
"  over immediates); an `ensures` only when it is proven (it is never checked at run time, also under\n" +
"  `--keep-proven-checks`); the body uses `+ - * +% -% *%`, `bit_and` / `bit_or` / `bit_xor` / `bit_not`, `bit_shl` /\n" +
"  `bit_shr` by an integer literal, `ct_select`, `ct_eq` and calls of other kernels; no `if`, `match`, comparison,\n" +
"  `and` / `or`, `/`, `%`, recursion. Every arithmetic result must be proven inside the 63-bit immediate range for\n" +
"  all immediate arguments (`[E0210]`). An entry guard faults when an argument is not an immediate. `ltv` re-derives\n" +
"  the ranges itself and validates the machine code; `tv_gate` mutates it. Limits: \"constant time\" is the absence of\n" +
"  secret-dependent branches, divisions and memory accesses in the instruction sequence; no timing is measured.\n" +
"- **Multi-ISA kernel back ends (Domain `#117`)**: `larm64.src` and `lriscv.src` compile the integer kernel fragment\n" +
"  (`int` functions, `+ - * / %`, comparisons, `and`/`or`, `if`, `let`, calls, `print`) to AArch64, RV64 and RV32\n" +
"  images; `ltv_multiarch.src` validates every function image against the source. No image is released before the\n" +
"  `lumec` front end accepted the same source (`[T0902]` with its diagnostic, `[T0903]` when `lumec` is missing); a\n" +
"  source outside the fragment is `[T0901]`. Real level: executed on `qemu-aarch64`, `qemu-riscv64` and the LumePuter\n" +
"  interpreter, not on silicon.\n" +
"- **Linear concurrency (Domain `#118`)**: a value sent with `chan_send_linear` cannot be used again (`[E0305]`);\n" +
"  `lock_acquire` out of rank order, an unreleased lock or a cycle of `actor_link` edges is rejected (`[E0306]`).\n" +
"- **Cryptography and TLS 1.3 (Domain `#119`, `use lcrypto_tls`)**: SHA-256/512, HMAC, HKDF, ChaCha20-Poly1305,\n" +
"  Ed25519, X25519, the TLS 1.3 key schedule, record layer and handshake state machine, all in Lume and checked\n" +
"  against the official vectors by `crypto_tls_gate`. For bulk data use the string API (binary strings, linear time,\n" +
"  memory of the output only): `lcs_sha256(s)`, `lcs_hmac_sha256(key, msg)`, `lcs_aead_seal(key32, nonce12, aad, p)`,\n" +
"  `lcs_aead_open(...)` -> `" + man_br("ok, plain") + "`, `lcs_chacha20`, `lcs_poly1305`, `lcs_hex` / `lcs_unhex`.\n" +
"  Incremental (a stream in pieces, same native speed): `lcs_sha256_init()`, `lcs_sha256_update(st, data)` -> st,\n" +
"  `lcs_sha256_final(st)` -> 32 bytes; `lcs_hmac_sha256_init(key)` / `_update(st, data)` / `_final(st)`; a state is a\n" +
"  value (an older one can still be continued or finished).\n" +
"  AES (FIPS 197) and AES-GCM (SP 800-38D) for QUIC Initial packets and the AES suites of TLS 1.3:\n" +
"  `lcs_aes128_ecb_encrypt(key16, block16)` (QUIC header protection), `lcs_aes128_gcm_seal(key16, nonce12, aad, p)`,\n" +
"  `lcs_aes128_gcm_open(...)` -> `" + man_br("ok, plain") + "`, the same with `aes256`. ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256\n" +
"  (`ecdsa_secp256r1_sha256`): `lcs_p256_verify(pub65, msg, sig_der)` -> 1 or 0, `lcs_p256_sign(priv32, msg)`\n" +
"  (RFC 6979 nonce), `lcs_p256_public(priv32)`, `_raw` forms with r || s. X25519 and Ed25519 (runtime routines\n" +
"  written in Lume): `lcs_x25519(k32, u32)`, `lcs_x25519_base(k32)`, `lcs_x25519_shared(k32, peer32)` -> `" + man_br("ok, secret") + "`,\n" +
"  `lcs_ed25519_public(seed32)`, `lcs_ed25519_sign(seed32, msg)`, `lcs_ed25519_verify(pk32, msg, sig64)`.\n" +
"  `ltv` adds `[C0010]`: the emitted code of a `@secret` function\n" +
"  may hold no conditional branch, division or memory access outside its frame, and neither may any routine it\n" +
"  reaches by `call` (the scan is transitive and names the call chain). Limits: tested, not formally\n" +
"  verified; a plain `@secret` function that uses `+` or a bit operation is rejected by `[C0010]` (its helpers\n" +
"  branch): write it as a constant-time kernel; X.509 path validation covers Ed25519 chains only (`lume x509 verify`,\n" +
"  Wave 14 section below).\n" +
"- **Incremental proof cache (Domain `#120`)**: one sealed record per function, keyed by the SHA-256 of its body,\n" +
"  contracts, callee interfaces and prover version. A tampered record is refused (`[PC0002]`), a module the prover\n" +
"  refutes is never stored (`[PC0003]`), `--require-all-hits` turns a miss into an error (`[PC0005]`).\n" +
"- **Neural cartridges (Domain `#121`)**: a `/ pure` integer function compiled to RV32IM words inside a\n" +
"  `.safetensors` file with the integer weights of one SwiGLU block; the forward pass over the weights of the file\n" +
"  must equal the native program and the LumePuter run. It is integer matrix arithmetic evaluated by this tool\n" +
"  chain, not a claim about a floating-point inference engine.\n" +
"- **Certificate binding (`lcert --check-source`)**: besides re-deriving every proof term, the kernel reads the\n" +
"  contracts of the source itself and refuses a certificate whose obligations are not the obligations of that file.\n" +
"- **Signed evidence**: `lume qualify` chains the sections of `QUALIFICATION_EVIDENCE.json` with SHA-256 and writes a\n" +
"  detached Ed25519 signature (`QUALIFICATION_EVIDENCE.sig.json`). The key is a developer key kept in a file on the\n" +
"  host (`/root/.lume/keys/qualification_ed25519.seed` or `--sign-key`): it shows who produced the file, it is not an\n" +
"  independent attestation.\n" +
"\n" +
"### Wave 14 Commands (stack bound, certificate checker, runtime-helper verifier, X.509, split bundle)\n" +
"  lume stack <src.src> [--fn <f,g>] [--asm <file.s>] [--critical] [--json]   Worst-case stack bytes of `@no_alloc` functions on the emitted x86-64 text (`lstack`)\n" +
"  lume smt-check <cert.smt2>... [--dir <dir>] [--raw] [--budget <n>] [--verbose]   Check the SMT-LIB2 certificates of `lume tv` with the native checker (`lsmt`)\n" +
"  lume tv-rt <src.src> [--asm <file.s>] [--canon]   Verify the emitted integer runtime helpers against their specification (`ltv_rt`)\n" +
"  lume x509 verify --chain <leaf.der,ca.der> --anchor <root.der> --now <unix-seconds>   X.509 v3 path validation (Ed25519); exit 0 valid, 3 invalid\n" +
"  lume x509 show <certificate>               Parsed fields of one certificate (DER or PEM) as JSON\n" +
"  lume entropy [--bytes <n>] [--source <device>] [--json]   Health-checked bytes of the OS random source\n" +
"  lume safety-envelope <kernel.src> --fn <f> --split <outdir>   Export the split bundle (the two channels as standalone programs)\n" +
"  lume safety-envelope --split-run --manifest <m> --seq <n> --args <a,b,..> --cmd-a <cmd> --cmd-b <cmd> [--cmd-c <cmd>] [--frame-timeout-ms <n>]\n" +
"                                             Vote over the exported programs through the frame protocol\n" +
"  lume safety-envelope --split-verify <manifest.json>   Re-hash the artifacts of a bundle against its manifest\n" +
"  lume safety-envelope <kernel.src> --fn <f> --args <a,b,..> [--inject <kind:params>] [--log <file>] [--work <dir>] [--ltv <path>] [--ltv-timeout-ms <n>]\n" +
"                                             The other protocol options of the lockstep run (`--inject` is a test instrument, recorded in the log)\n" +
"  lume tv-rt-gate [--stride <n>]             Mutation gate of `ltv_rt` (`tv_rt_gate`)\n" +
"  lume smt-cert-gate [--require-z3] [--solver <none>] [--chameleon] [--sites <n>] [--corpus <dir>]   Gate of `lsmt` (`smt_cert_gate`; z3 is the ground truth when installed)\n" +
"  lume lcaas-scale-gate [--full] [--modes <a,b>] [--fams <x,y>] [--reps <k>] [--timeout <ms>] [--lcaas <path>]   Complexity regression gate of `lcaas` (`lcaas_scale_gate`)\n" +
"  lume cli-parity                            The command-line parity gate alone (needs a source checkout)\n" +
"\n" +
"- **`lstack` (worst-case stack)**: for each `@no_alloc` function, the maximum over every path of the control-flow\n" +
"  graph of the EMITTED text of the bytes used below the entry `%rsp`, return addresses and callees included; the\n" +
"  runtime routines the function reaches are analysed by the same rules, not assumed. Two bounds are reported:\n" +
"  `all paths` (often `unbounded`, because the slow path of `+` can box its result) and `proven`, which removes\n" +
"  exactly the slow-path edges that the `[E0210]` range proofs make dead and lists each removal as an assumption.\n" +
"  Limits: the proven bound is conditional on those proofs (the tool does not re-prove them); a caller outside\n" +
"  `@no_alloc` code can pass a boxed integer; signal frames are outside the model; a call cycle or a path into the\n" +
"  allocator is `unbounded`. Exit status 3 when a function is rejected.\n" +
"- **`lsmt` (certificate checker)**: a decision procedure that shares no code with `ltv`, `lcert` or the compiler\n" +
"  (polynomial normal form, congruence, case split over the integers). Only `unsat` passes: `unknown`,\n" +
"  `unsupported`, `malformed` and `forged` are failures. In certificate mode the script must have the exact shape of\n" +
"  an `ltv` claim (`--raw` refutes any script of the subset). Limits: `unsat` establishes that the certificate TEXT\n" +
"  is a valid refutation, not that the text describes the source and the assembly (that binding is `ltv`'s); the\n" +
"  procedure is incomplete by design (budget, non-linear terms as opaque atoms).\n" +
"- **`ltv_rt` (runtime helpers)**: the integer helpers `ltv` takes as axioms (`mkint`, `addv`, `__rt_sub`,\n" +
"  `__rt_mul`, `__rt_div`, `__rt_mod`, the wrapping forms, `cmpv`, `eqv`, the unboxing helpers) are verified on the\n" +
"  emitted text by symbolic execution over all inputs of the modelled cases; anything outside the model is a\n" +
"  rejection. What stays an axiom: the allocator contract, the trap tail that does not return, and the listed\n" +
"  x86-64 facts. `--canon` adds the experiment that shows which helpers rely on the canonical-form invariant.\n" +
"- **X.509 and entropy (`use lcrypto_tls`)**: `lume x509 verify` validates a path (leaf first, each certificate\n" +
"  issued by the next) against pinned anchors at the instant `--now`: strict DER, validity periods,\n" +
"  basicConstraints, keyUsage, path length, name chaining and Ed25519 signatures. Limits: Ed25519 only (RSA and\n" +
"  ECDSA certificates are refused), at most 8 certificates, no host name matching, no revocation, no name\n" +
"  constraints or policies; the tool has no clock, the caller supplies `--now`. `lume entropy` reads `/dev/urandom`\n" +
"  and releases bytes only when the health checks pass (all zero, all equal, repetition count, adaptive proportion,\n" +
"  identical consecutive reads): they detect a dead or stuck source, they do NOT measure or certify entropy.\n" +
"- **Clean-room channel B**: the monitor channel of `lume safety-envelope` shares no front end with `lumec`. Its\n" +
"  lexer, parser, typed checker and RV32IM code generator are written from the language definition inside\n" +
"  `lsafety_envelope.src`, which does not link the compiler (the gate checks that on the bundle of the tool), and\n" +
"  it compiles every `requires` / `ensures` into a run-time check. Where the specification and `lumec` differ the\n" +
"  kernel is refused. Limits: both channels are given the same kernel text and the same language definition (a\n" +
"  wrong specification is implemented twice); the same team wrote both; integer / bool kernel fragment only; i32\n" +
"  monitor domain.\n" +
"- **Split bundle** (`docs/41-safety-envelope-split-bundle.md`): `--split` writes channel A as x86-64, AArch64 and\n" +
"  RV64 programs, channel B as a bare-metal RV32IM image, and `manifest.json` with the size and SHA-256 of each.\n" +
"  `--split-run` sends one request frame to each command and votes on the response frames (CRC, sequence, kernel id,\n" +
"  argument echo, status, exact result); a missing, late, malformed or replayed frame is a trip, latched in the\n" +
"  event log. Real level: executed on this host and under QEMU (`qemu-aarch64`, `qemu-riscv64`,\n" +
"  `qemu-system-riscv32`), not on silicon; two processes on one host are not two boards; the voter and its log are\n" +
"  a single point. The AArch64 / RV64 programs exist only for kernels inside the `lkir` fragment (the manifest\n" +
"  records why otherwise).\n" +
"- **Driver cache and concurrent runs**: `lume build`, `lume run`, `lume test`, `lume check`, `lume prove` and\n" +
"  `lume certify` keep their cache in `build/driver-cache` of the checkout (hash-checked entries, published by\n" +
"  rename), use per-process scratch names and write nothing under the home directory, so several drivers can work\n" +
"  in one checkout. The key of a cached bundle is the SHA-256 of every bundled module.\n" +
"- **`lume pack`**: the body is the LZ4 block format; the file starts with a 20-byte header (magic `LZ1`, original\n" +
"  length, checksum) and is not an LZ4 frame.\n" +
"\n" +
"## 8.4 Universal Module Orchestrator (`LumeSynapse`) & Proactive Memory\n" +
"- `lume synapse <file.src>` (or `lume orchestrate <file.src>`): Coordinates all Lume\n" +
"  organs (`lmod`, `lumec`, `lasm`, `lcaas`, `lcert`, `ltest`, `lprotect`, `lsentience`)\n" +
"  via the shared blackboard (`synapse_bus.json`) of the sentience memory under the home directory.\n" +
"  Since Wave 14 the plain commands (`lume build`, `lume run`, `lume test`, `lume check`, `lume prove`,\n" +
"  `lume certify`) do not write that memory: their cache is `build/driver-cache` inside the checkout, and\n" +
"  `lume check` and `lume prove` share one cached oracle answer per bundle.\n" +
"- `lume recall <file.src>`: Queries the O(1) content-addressed proactive memory cache\n" +
"  protected by `.sha256` cryptographic anti-tamper seals (up to 91x faster proofs and\n" +
"  20x faster builds).\n" +
"- `lume self-prove` (or `lume prove-all` / `lume verify-all` / `lume self prove`): Runs\n" +
"  the proof batteries (`LumeCompiler-Embedded-OmniProof-v4`; every count in the JSON is measured by the run) inside\n" +
"  the compiled Lume driver with zero external scripts (`std.net`, `std.gfx`,\n" +
"  `lume_crypto_blockchain_engine`, `lume_reversa_engine`, `lume_pingora_proxy_engine`,\n" +
"  `lume_egm_engine`, `lume_ncm_engine`, `lume_opentpu_engine`, `lume_continuum_nexus_engine`,\n" +
"  `lume_quantum_nexus_engine`, `lchameleon`, `lsentience`, `lmanual`, `KerneLume` Bare-Metal OS,\n" +
"  `[K0005]`/`[K0006]`/`[C0009]`/SRA guards, and `MANIFEST.sha256`: 700 formal obligations +\n" +
"  162 unit tests + 99 verified toolchain artifacts + 112 autonomous domains + 17 LumePuter modules).\n"

fn man_en_examples() = "# CHAPTER 9: 6 COPY-PASTE WORKING EXAMPLES FOR HUMANS & AI\n\n" +
"## Example 1: Recursion, ADTs & Pattern Matching (`list_demo.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"fn map_double(xs) = match xs\n" +
"    Nil        => Nil\n" +
"    Cons(h, t) => Cons(h * 2, map_double(t))\n\n" +
"fn sum_all(xs) = match xs\n" +
"    Nil        => 0\n" +
"    Cons(h, t) => h + sum_all(t)\n\n" +
"fn test_double_sum() = sum_all(map_double(Cons(3, Cons(7, Nil)))) == 20\n" +
"print str(sum_all(map_double(Cons(10, Cons(20, Nil)))))\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## Example 2: Formal Verification with `requires`, `ensures` & `law` (`bank_proof.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"fn safe_transfer(sender: int, receiver: int, amount: int) -> int\n" +
"  requires sender >= amount and amount >= 0 and receiver >= 0\n" +
"  ensures result == sender + receiver\n" +
"= (sender - amount) + (receiver + amount)\n\n" +
"law transfer_conserves_total(s: int, r: int, a: int) = ((s - a) + (r + a)) == (s + r)\n" +
"print str(safe_transfer(500, 200, 150))\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## Example 3: File I/O, SHA-256 & Dictionary Map (`hash_kv.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"use fs_sha256_file\n" +
"use map\n\n" +
"fn run_demo() =\n" +
"    let m0 = map_new() in\n" +
"    let m1 = map_put(m0, \"creator\", lc_sha256(\"Ricardo Bueno\")) in\n" +
"    map_get_or(m1, \"creator\", \"missing\")\n\n" +
"print run_demo()\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## Example 4: B+Tree ACID Database & SQL Query (`db_demo.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"use db\n\n" +
"fn run_db() =\n" +
"    let d0 = db_open(2) in\n" +
"    let tx = db_put(db_begin_tx(d0), 1, 100, 1) in\n" +
"    let d1 = db_commit_tx(tx) in\n" +
"    db_read(d1, 1, 0)\n\n" +
"print str(run_db())\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## Example 5: Cryptographic Custody, PoW Mining & DeFi AMM (`crypto_demo.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"use lume_crypto_blockchain_engine\n\n" +
"fn crypto_sha256_rounds(msg: str) = crypto_hmac_sha256(\"lume-key\", msg)\n" +
"print crypto_sha256_rounds(\"block-0\")\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## Example 6: Freestanding Hardware / Kernel Entry (`kernel_demo.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"@bound(cycles: 128)\n" +
"fn rtc_bcd_to_bin(bcd: int) -> int\n" +
"  requires bcd >= 0 and bcd <= 153\n" +
"  ensures result >= 0\n" +
"= ((bcd / 16) * 10) + (bcd % 16)\n\n" +
"print str(rtc_bcd_to_bin(35))\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## Example 7: Universal Chameleon Polyglot Interop (`chameleon_demo.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"use lchameleon\n\n" +
"fn run_chameleon_demo() =\n" +
"    let ok = chameleon_verify_boundary(1, 1, 1, 64, 4096) in\n" +
"    let r = chameleon_adapt_ecosystem(\"rust\") in\n" +
"    str(ok) + \":\" + r.id\n\n" +
"print run_chameleon_demo()\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## Example 8: LumePuter & LumePU In-Weights Neural VM & NPU (`lumeputer_demo.src`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"use lchameleon\n\n" +
"fn run_lumeputer_demo() =\n" +
"    let relu_val = lumeputer_swiglu_exact_relu_unit(42, 1, 20) in\n" +
"    let ram_cell = lumeputer_deltanet_ram_step_exact(99, 777, 1) in\n" +
"    let vx_mac = lumepu_vx_vmat_row_mac_exact(10, 4, 8, 64) in\n" +
"    let layers = lumeputer_compile_rv32_vx_to_weights_layers(64, 1, 1) in\n" +
"    str(relu_val) + \":\" + str(ram_cell) + \":\" + str(vx_mac) + \":\" + str(layers)\n\n" +
"print run_lumeputer_demo()\n" +
"```\n"

fn man_en_errors() = "# CHAPTER 10: COMPILER DIAGNOSTIC CODES & HOW TO FIX THEM\n\n" +
"| Code      | Category             | Meaning & How to Fix |\n" +
"|-----------|----------------------|----------------------|\n" +
"| `[P0002]` | Parser / Syntax      | Unexpected token or nested unbraced `match`. Move `match` to top-level helper `fn f(x) = match x ...` or wrap in braces `match x " + man_br(" ... ") + "`, and verify pure LF (`\\n`) line endings. |\n" +
"| `[R0200]` | Name Resolution      | Call to undefined function or variable. Check spelling or add `use <module>` at top of file. |\n" +
"| `[R0201]` | Name Resolution      | A function reuses the name of a runtime routine (`count`, `at`, ...) or a prefix reserved for it (`__rt_`, `__gc_`, `__lume_`, `__c_`, `__k_`, `__r_`, `__isr_`, `__cpu_`, `__krn_`, `__net_`). Rename it. |\n" +
"| `[T0300]` | Tensor Shape         | Tensor shape mismatch: an argument dimension differs from the parameter's, or the branches of an `if` disagree. Reshape the tensor. |\n" +
"| `[T2001]` | Type Check           | An operator applied to incompatible types (`int + str`, `money[BRL] + money[USD]`). Convert both operands to the same type. |\n" +
"| `[T2002]` | Type Check           | A function returns a type other than the one it declares. Fix the body or the declared return type. |\n" +
"| `[E0200]` | Algebraic Effects    | Impure operation (`io`, `fs`, `net`, `arena_new`, `embed`) called inside a `/ pure` function. Remove `/ pure` or add the required effect to the function signature. |\n" +
"| `[O0001]` | Ownership / Borrow   | Use-after-move, double-close of file handle, or conflicting mutable borrow (`mut`). Clone or restructure ownership scope. |\n" +
"| `[V0001]` | Contract / Law Proof | `requires`/`ensures` contract or `law` refuted by `QF_LIA` solver. Inspect the printed counterexample or run `lume heal <file.src>`. |\n" +
"| `[V0002]` | WCET Cycle Bound     | Function exceeds `@bound(cycles: N)` budget or uses unbounded recursion in `@interrupt`. |\n" +
"| `[I0003]` | Polyglot / C Interop | Unsafe or unsupported foreign declaration in `lume adapt c` or `lchameleon` (`unverified[T] -> verified[T]`). Add explicit `QF_LIA` bounds or `@repr(c)`. |\n" +
"| `[I0275]` | WASM Sandbox         | A WebAssembly module handed to the capability sandbox imports an ungranted host capability (`path_open`, `sock_*`), declares memory outside `1..16` pages, or is malformed. |\n" +
"| `[C0271]` | Comptime Embed       | `comptime embed(\"...\")`: the path is not a string, is empty, contains `..`, or names a missing file. |\n" +
"| `[D0273]` | Table Schema         | `comptime table_schema(T)`: `T` is not a nominal record type, or a column has an unsupported type or an invalid money currency. |\n" +
"| `[K0005]` | Bare-Metal W^X / DMA | `mmio_volatile_write*`, `mem_copy`, or `mem_set` targets `.text`/`.rodata` (`[0x8000..0x3FFFF]`), including symbolic/affine `base + off`. Use a safe DMA RAM buffer (`>= 0x40000`). |\n" +
"| `[K0006]` | Kernel Stack Safety  | Unbounded mutual recursion cycle (`f -> g -> f`) in `@freestanding` / `kernel_boot_entry` module. Use tail-loop state or bounded iteration. |\n" +
"| `[C0009]` | Constant-Time Crypto | Secret-dependent `if`/`match` branch, variable-latency `/` or `%`, short-circuit `and`/`or`, or secret-indexed memory lookup. Secrets are parameters named `secret` or `secret_*`; in a function whose name starts with `ct_` every parameter is a secret (only the `secret*` ones when it has some), so `fn ct_size(n) = if n == 0 then 1 else 2` fails and `fn size(n) = ...` passes. Use bitwise XOR/OR mask accumulation, or drop the `ct_` prefix when the function handles no secret. |\n" +
"| `[C0010]` | Machine Constant-Time | `lume tv`: the emitted code of a `@secret fn`, or of a routine it reaches by `call`, holds a conditional branch, a division or a memory access outside frame and stack. Write the function as a constant-time kernel (`@secret` + `@no_alloc`). |\n" +
"| `[C0011]` | Constant-Time Kernel | A `@secret` + `@no_alloc` function has a `requires`, an unproven `ensures`, a conditional, comparison, `/` or `%`, a shift by a non-literal, recursion, a non-`int` type or a call of a function that is not a kernel. Use masks, `ct_select(mask, a, b)` and `ct_eq(a, b)`. |\n" +
"| `[L0001]` | Lexer / Assembler    | Unterminated string literal in a source file (close it with a double quote); `lasm` uses the same code for an instruction or directive it does not know. |\n" +
"| `[L0010]` | Link                 | A symbol is defined twice in one image, which would otherwise send calls to the wrong routine. |\n" +
"| `[L0002]` | String Escape        | Unknown escape sequence in string literal (valid escapes: `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\b`, `\\f`, `\\0`, `\\xHH`, `\\'`, `\\\"`, `\\\\`, `\\{`, `\\}`, `\\$`). |\n" +
"| `[W0002]` | P33 Secret Scanner   | Hardcoded private key/token detected before binary emission; move secrets out of source. |\n" +
"| `[W0003]` | Duplicate Name       | One name is defined in two modules of the same program (a warning: each module keeps its own). Rename one, make it `priv fn`, or write `module.name` where both are visible. |\n" +
"| `[W0004]` | f64 Meets int        | An arithmetic operator mixes an f64 and an int (a warning: the int is converted at run time). Write `f64(n)` to say so, or `f64_int(x)` for an int result. |\n" +
"| `[W0005]` | Deprecated           | The function is marked `## Deprecated: <message>` (comment directly above it) and is called from another module. It keeps working for at least one whole MINOR release (docs/STABILITY.md); move to the replacement the message names. |\n"

## ============================================================================
## PORTUGUESE CHAPTERS (PT-BR — MANUAL COMPLETO PARA HUMANOS EM PORTUGUES)
## ============================================================================

fn man_pt_index() = "# ============================================================================\n" +
"# LINGUAGEM LUME — MANUAL INTERNO PARA HUMANOS E IA (v1.2.0 / Onda 10)\n" +
"# Edicao 2026 | Zero-C Self-Hosted | \"Lume gera Lume\"\n" +
"# ============================================================================\n\n" +
"Bem-vindo ao Manual Interno da Lume! Embora a Lume tenha sido projetada como\n" +
"AI-First (onde a propria linguagem sintetiza, prova e evolui codigo), ela foi\n" +
"construida para que qualquer programador humano possa programar com clareza,\n" +
"seguranca matematica e controle total da maquina.\n\n" +
"## COMO USAR ESTE MANUAL NO TERMINAL\n" +
"  lume manual --pt                Mostrar este indice em Portugues (pt-BR)\n" +
"  lume manual --pt <capitulo>     Ler um capitulo (ex: lume manual --pt sintaxe)\n" +
"  lume manual --pt tudo           Ler todos os 10 capitulos completos de uma vez\n" +
"  lume manual <chapter>           Ler o manual em Ingles (EN)\n" +
"  lume manual --json [capitulo]   Emitir manual estruturado em JSON\n" +
"  lume manual --pt --export <f>   Exportar o manual completo em Markdown (.md)\n" +
"  lume help <capitulo>            Atalho direto para qualquer capitulo\n\n" +
"## PARA QUEM PROGRAMA E PARA IAs\n" +
"  lume manual --pt referencia   Referencia factual: so o que funciona hoje, estado de cada builtin e modulo,\n" +
"                                cada exemplo executado pela bateria de testes (comece por aqui)\n" +
"  lume manual --pt visao        Material de visao e pesquisa (os capitulos 1-10 o misturam com a referencia)\n" +
"\n" +
"## CAPITULOS DO MANUAL (10 CAPITULOS)\n" +
"  1. visao-geral (overview)   Arquitetura (.lume vs .src), Inicio Rapido e Fluxo\n" +
"  2. sintaxe     (syntax)     Gramatica Completa, fn/type/match/let e Regras do Compilador\n" +
"  3. tipos       (types)      Tipos Primitivos, Registros, ADTs, Ownership, Decimal, Tensor\n" +
"  4. contratos   (contracts)  Verificacao Formal (requires, ensures, law, QF_LIA, WCET)\n" +
"  5. efeitos     (effects)    Efeitos Algebricos (/ pure), Arenas de Memoria e E-Capsules\n" +
"  6. biblioteca  (stdlib)     Biblioteca Padrao e Modulos Soberanos (`lume manual --pt camaleao`)\n" +
"  7. alvos       (targets)    27 Alvos Universais, MIR SSA, APK/IPA/ISO/UEFI e RTL\n" +
"  8. comandos    (commands)   Guia Completo de Comandos CLI (`lume chameleon` / `lume camaleao`)\n" +
"  9. exemplos    (examples)   6 Programas Completos + Exemplo 7 (`chameleon_demo.src`)\n" +
" 10. erros       (errors)     Tabela de Codigos de Erro ([P0002]..[W0002]) e Solucoes\n"

fn man_pt_overview() = "# CAPITULO 1: VISAO GERAL E INICIO RAPIDO PARA HUMANOS\n\n" +
"## 1.1 O Que e a Linguagem Lume?\n" +
"Lume e uma linguagem de programacao auto-hospedada (Zero-C: o compilador `lumec`,\n" +
"o montador `lasm` e o driver `lcli` sao escritos 100% em Lume e compilam a si\n" +
"mesmos de forma bit-identica `stage2 == stage3`).\n\n" +
"Ela possui duas camadas de sintaxe:\n" +
"1. `.src` (Lume-Core): A sintaxe funcional/expressiva canonica compilada diretamente\n" +
"   pelo compilador nativo `lumec`. E a forma mais direta e recomendada para programar.\n" +
"2. `.lume` (Surface Lume): Sintaxe de blocos/indentacao que desce para Lume-Core.\n\n" +
"## 1.2 Seu Primeiro Programa em 30 Segundos\n" +
"1. Crie o arquivo `ola.src` (sempre com quebras de linha LF `\\n`):\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn dobro_positivo(x: int) -> int\n" +
"     requires x >= 0\n" +
"     ensures result >= x\n" +
"   = x * 2\n\n" +
"   fn test_dobro() = dobro_positivo(21) == 42\n\n" +
"   print \"Resultado: \" + str(dobro_positivo(21))\n" +
"   ```\n" +
"2. Executar imediatamente:\n" +
"   `lume run ola.src`             -> imprime `Resultado: 42`\n" +
"3. Rodar os testes unitarios (`fn test_*()`):\n" +
"   `lume test ola.src`            -> executa todas as funcoes `test_*`\n" +
"4. Provar matematicamente os contratos (`requires`/`ensures`):\n" +
"   `lume prove ola.src`           -> gera a prova formal `QF_LIA` em JSON\n" +
"5. Compilar um executavel nativo independente (ELF64 / PE64):\n" +
"   `lume build ola.src -o ola`\n"

fn man_pt_syntax() = "# CAPITULO 2: SINTAXE, GRAMATICA E REGRAS DO COMPILADOR\n\n" +
"## 2.1 Declaracoes de Topo em Arquivos `.src`\n" +
"Em um arquivo `.src`, tudo no nivel de topo deve ser uma das seguintes declaracoes:\n" +
"- `use <modulo>`               Importa um modulo (ex: `use fs`, `use map`, `use db`).\n" +
"- `type Nome = ...`            Define um Tipo Algebrico (ADT) ou registro.\n" +
"- `fn nome(a, b) = expr`       Define uma funcao.\n" +
"- `pub fn nome(a, b) = expr`   Define uma funcao publica exportada.\n" +
"- `priv fn nome(a, b) = expr`  Funcao privada do modulo: outros modulos nao a chamam e ela nunca colide com os nomes deles.\n" +
"- `fn f(x: any) -> any = x`    `any` desliga a checagem estatica: qualquer valor serve, o runtime confere o uso.\n" +
"- `const NOME: T = expr`       Define uma constante de modulo (disponivel em funcoes e contratos).\n" +
"- `law nome(a: int) = expr`    Define uma lei matematica universal provada pelo compilador.\n" +
"- `print <expr>`               Ponto de entrada executavel do programa.\n\n" +
"## 2.1.1 Palavras Reservadas e Nomes com Significado Especial\n" +
"- Palavras-chave (nunca sao nomes): `if then else elif let in var mut match not and or own with spawn do defer errdefer`\n" +
"  `comptime quote splice scope shard fn pub use as type const law print requires ensures true false`.\n" +
"- Nome com inicial maiuscula e construtor (`Nil`, `Cons`, as variantes do seu `type`), nunca funcao ou variavel.\n" +
"- Builtins do runtime (`count`, `at`, `slice`, `ord`, `str`, `buf_get`, ... veja `lume manual --pt biblioteca`) e os prefixos\n" +
"  `__rt_` e `__lume_` pertencem ao runtime: uma funcao com esse nome e recusada com [R0201].\n" +
"- `ct_` no inicio do nome de uma funcao torna todos os parametros segredos (so os `secret` / `secret_*`, se houver):\n" +
"  `if`, `match`, `/`, `%`, `and` / `or` ou indice de tabela sobre eles da [C0009]. Parametros chamados `secret` ou\n" +
"  `secret_*` sao segredos em qualquer funcao.\n" +
"- Funcoes `test_*` sao as que o `lume test` roda; uma `pub fn` sem `test_` de mesmo nome recebe o aviso P35.\n" +
"- `grad`, `value_and_grad`, `jvp`, `vjp` sao os operadores de autodiff: uma chamada deles sobre uma funcao e\n" +
"  derivada ([N0400]); nao de esses nomes as suas funcoes.\n" +
"- Em `ensures`: `result` e o valor devolvido e `old(x)` o valor de x na entrada. `_` como corpo e um buraco para\n" +
"  sintese pelo comando intent. `kernel_boot_entry` e a entrada de um kernel `@freestanding` ([K0006]).\n" +
"- Atributos: `@export(\"C\")`, `@secret`, `@no_alloc`, `@bound(cycles: N)`, `@interrupt`, `@freestanding`, `@repr(c)`.\n" +
"- Modulos: `use m as a` faz `a.nome` ser o `nome` de m; um nome definido em dois modulos importados fica separado\n" +
"  como `nome__m`, e o uso sem qualificar e erro de ambiguidade com arquivo:linha:coluna.\n" +
"- `use std/NOME` nomeia o modulo NOME da biblioteca padrao mesmo quando o projeto tem um NOME.src (`use std/h264`).\n" +
"\n" +
"## 2.2 Expressoes, Desestruturacao e Operadores Ergonomicos (DX 10/10)\n" +
"- Variavel local (`let..in`): `let a = 10 in let b = 20 in a + b`\n" +
"- Desestruturacao de tupla:   `let (a, b) = (10, 20) in a + b`\n" +
"- Desestruturacao de record:  `let " + man_br("x, y") + " = ponto in x + y`\n" +
"- Operador Pipe (`|>`):       `x |> etapa1(5) |> etapa2`\n" +
"- Record Update (`with`):     `" + man_br(" estado with contador: estado.contador + 1 ") + "`\n" +
"- Interpolacao de Strings:    `f\"valor=" + man_br("x") + "\"`, `\"valor=$" + man_br("x") + "\"` ou `\"valor=" + man_br("x") + "\"`\n" +
"                              (JSON bruto `\"{\\\"a\\\":{\\\"b\\\":1}}\"` preserva todas as chaves; escape chaves\n" +
"                              literais com `\"\\" + man_br("x") + "\"`, `\"" + man_br(man_br("x")) + "\"` ou `\"custo: \\$" + man_br("x") + "\"`; escapes `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\b`, `\\f`, `\\0`, `\\xHH`, `\\'`, `\\\"`, `\\\\`)\n" +
"- Condicional (`if..then..else` ou chaves): `if x > 0 then 1 else 0` ou `if x > 0 " + man_br(" 1 ") + " else " + man_br(" 0 ") + "`\n" +
"- Operadores logicos (curto-circuito): `a == 1 and b == 2`, `x < 0 or x > 10`, `not (a == b)` (`not` tem precedencia menor que `==`/`<`)\n" +
"- Aritmetica: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%`\n" +
"- Comparacao: `==`, `!=` (igualdade estrutural em pilha `O(1)` para listas/ADTs/records profundos), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`\n" +
"- Registros (Structs): `let p = " + man_br("x: 10, y: 20") + " in p.x + p.y`\n" +
"- Atualizacao: `" + man_br("e with f: v") + "` copia trocando campos; e e qualquer expressao (nome, chamada,\n" +
"  campo `r.b`, `(e)`); campo que o registro nao tem e `[T2101]`, tambem quando o registro vem de uma\n" +
"  funcao ou dos dois ramos de um if\n" +
"- Palavras reservadas (`if`, `let`, `var`, `match`, `with`, `fn` e as demais) nao podem nomear funcao, variavel\n" +
"  ou parametro (P0002 na propria declaracao)\n" +
"- `+` soma dois inteiros ou junta duas strs; nada e convertido implicitamente (`\"total: \" + str(n)`, [T0604]);\n" +
"  listas se juntam com `seq_concat(xs, ys)` (`use seq`), e `xs + [d]` e recusado no `lume check` e na compilacao\n" +
"- Literais de lista e ADTs: `[]` (`Nil`), `[1, 2, 3]` (`Cons(1, Cons(2, Cons(3, Nil)))`), `count([1, 2, 3]) == 3`\n" +
"- Comentarios: `## Comentarios comecam com dois sustenidos`\n\n" +
"## 2.3 Reconhecimento de Padroes (`match` — DX 10/10)\n" +
"Voce pode usar `match` em qualquer lugar (corpo de funcao, `let ... in`, `if`, argumentos de chamada, campos de record e bracos de `match`):\n" +
"1. No topo do corpo de uma funcao:\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn soma_lista(xs) = match xs\n" +
"       Nil        => 0\n" +
"       Cons(h, t) => h + soma_lista(t)\n" +
"   ```\n" +
"2. Aninhado por indentacao dentro de `let ... in`, `if`, argumentos de funcao ou bracos de `match`:\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn cabeca_ou_zero(xs) =\n" +
"       let y = match xs\n" +
"           Nil        => 0\n" +
"           Cons(h, _) => h\n" +
"       in y + 1\n" +
"   ```\n" +
"3. Inline com chaves `match expr " + man_br(" Padrao => corpo, ... ") + "`:\n" +
"   ```lume\n" +
"   fn tamanho_um(xs) = let r = match xs " + man_br(" Nil => 0, Cons(_, Nil) => 1, Cons(_, _) => 2 ") + " in r\n" +
"   ```\n" +
"REGRA DE OURO:\n" +
"1. Salve sempre seus arquivos com quebra de linha LF (`\\n`), nunca CRLF (`\\r\\n`).\n" +
"2. Qualquer Aridade de Parametros + TCO: O codegen nativo SysV AMD64 (`05_codegen.src`)\n" +
"   passa os primeiros 6 parametros em `%rdi, %rsi, %rdx, %rcx, %r8, %r9` e parametros 7+\n" +
"   na pilha com otimizacao de tail-call (`jmp`) segura para trocas de argumentos.\n" +
"3. Validacao Fail-Closed de Patterns e Bindings: Nomes duplicados em parametros/patterns/\n" +
"   desestruturacao, patterns decimais (`1.5 =>`) e `match` aninhado sem chaves na mesma linha\n" +
"   falham fechado com `[P0002]`.\n" +
"4. Nunca edite `compiler/stage1/lumec.src` diretamente: edite `compiler/stage1/lume/NN_*.src`\n" +
"   e execute `build/bin/lume_make amalgamate`.\n"

fn man_pt_types() = "# CAPITULO 3: SISTEMA DE TIPOS, OWNERSHIP, FINANCAS E TENSORES\n\n" +
"## 3.1 Tipos Fundamentais\n" +
"- `int`               Inteiro de 64 bits com sinal\n" +
"- `bool`              Booleano (`true` / `false`, ou `1` / `0` em Lume-Core)\n" +
"- `str`               String UTF-8 imutavel com tamanho em cache `O(1)` (`count(s)`)\n" +
"- `bytes`             Buffer de bytes seguro com verificacao de limites (`std.bytes`)\n" +
"- `List[T]`           Lista imutavel (`Nil` | `Cons(h, t)`)\n" +
"- `Option[T]`         `None` | `Some(v)`\n" +
"- `Result[T, E]`      `Ok(v)` | `Err(e)`\n\n" +
"## 3.2 Tipos de Dados Algebricos (`type`)\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"type Pagamento =\n" +
"    Pix(int)\n" +
"  | Cartao(int, int)\n\n" +
"fn taxa(p) = match p\n" +
"    Pix(valor)            => 0\n" +
"    Cartao(valor, tarifa) => tarifa\n" +
"```\n\n" +
"## 3.3 Tipos Financeiros e de Dados (`decimal`, `money`, `table`)\n" +
"- `decimal(p, s)`     Decimal exato de ponto fixo (sem erros de ponto flutuante IEEE 754).\n" +
"                      Um literal com ponto (`1.5`, `0.10`) e decimal; imprime como escrito e\n" +
"                      continua exato por parametros, listas e registros; `1.20 == 1.2` e verdadeiro.\n" +
"- `f64`               Ponto flutuante IEEE 754 (builtins, sem `use`): `f64(x)` de int, decimal, f64\n" +
"                      ou texto; `+ - * /` e comparacoes; `str`/`print` dao o texto mais curto que\n" +
"                      volta ao mesmo double; `f64_str(x, n)` com n casas; `f64_int`, `f64_floor`,\n" +
"                      `f64_ceil`, `f64_round`, `f64_sqrt`, `f64_abs`, `f64_sin`, `f64_cos`, `f64_tan`,\n" +
"                      `f64_atan2`, `f64_exp`, `f64_log`, `f64_log10`, `f64_pow`, `f64_is_nan`,\n" +
"                      `f64_bits`, `f64_from_bits`. Comparar com NaN para o programa (use f64_is_nan).\n" +
"                      Um parametro declarado `x: f64` converte o argumento com f64(x) (entao `3.0`\n" +
"                      funciona ali). `use math`: sqrt exp log log10 pow sin cos tan atan2 floor ceil\n" +
"                      round abs_f fmin fmax tofloat is_nan is_inf, f32(x) (precisao simples, empate\n" +
"                      para o par), buf_f32_get(b, off) / buf_f32_set(b, off, x). [W0004]: int com f64.\n" +
"- `money[BRL]`        Dinheiro tipado por moeda (`money[BRL]`, `money[USD]`). Somar moedas\n" +
"                      diferentes sem conversao explicita gera erro em tempo de compilacao!\n" +
"- `table[T]`          Tabela relacional tipada com suporte a `persist table` (WAL duravel).\n\n" +
"## 3.4 Tensores Verificados e Diferenciacao Automatica (`tensor`)\n" +
"- `tensor[f32, 64, 128]` Verifica dimensoes em tempo de compilacao (`[T0300]`).\n" +
"- Suporta autodiff reverso e direto (`grad`, `value_and_grad`, `jvp`, `vjp`).\n\n" +
"## 3.5 Ownership, Borrow Checker e Capacidades de Hardware\n" +
"- `own T` (posse linear), `ref T` (emprestimo compartilhado), `mut T` (emprestimo exclusivo)\n" +
"  verificados em tempo de compilacao (`[O0001]`..`[O0030]`) com reuso Perceus.\n" +
"- Capacidades lineares de hardware para sistemas operacionais: `cap[Page]`, `cap[Port]`, `cap[Irq]`.\n"

fn man_pt_contracts() = "# CAPITULO 4: CONTRATOS, LEIS MATEMATICAS E VERIFICACAO FORMAL\n\n" +
"## 4.1 Pre-condicoes (`requires`) e Pos-condicoes (`ensures`)\n" +
"Qualquer funcao em Lume pode carregar contratos provados matematicamente pelo solver\n" +
"`QF_LIA` embutido no compilador:\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"fn sacar(saldo: int, valor: int) -> int\n" +
"  requires saldo >= valor and valor > 0\n" +
"  ensures result >= 0 and result < saldo\n" +
"= saldo - valor\n" +
"```\n" +
"Se houver qualquer possibilidade de `result < 0`, o compilador rejeita o codigo com\n" +
"`[V0001]` e mostra o contraexemplo exato!\n\n" +
"## 4.2 Leis Universais (`law`) e Idioma de Implicacao Logica\n" +
"```lume\n" +
"law simetria_soma(a: int, b: int) = (a + b) == (b + a)\n" +
"law implicacao_clamp(x: int, lo: int, hi: int) =\n" +
"  if lo <= hi then clamp(x, lo, hi) >= lo else 1 == 1\n" +
"```\n" +
"- Idioma de Implicacao (`if P then Q else 1 == 1`): Expresse implicacoes logicas $P \\implies Q$\n" +
"  dentro de `law` usando `if P then Q else 1 == 1`, reduzindo diretamente para ramos\n" +
"  decidiveis `QF_LIA` tanto no `lcaas.src` quanto no kernel independente `lcert.src`.\n" +
"- Produtos limitados (QF_NIA por relaxacao): `x * y` com os dois fatores limitados nos `requires` fica preso\n" +
"  pelas quatro desigualdades de McCormick: `dt * taxa / 1000` com `dt <= 60000` e `taxa <= 10000000000` prova\n" +
"  `result <= 600000000000` (`lume prove`, e `lume certify` emite o selo); fator sem limite ou limite falso continua\n" +
"  sem prova ou refutado com contraexemplo. O limite pode vir dos `requires` ou do caminho (`if a >= 4398046511104\n" +
"  then lim else a * p / 1000`), tambem dentro de um `let`; valem limites ate 2^62. Um fator pode ser uma expressao\n" +
"  linear limitada (`(255 - c) * alfa`) e a divisao pode ser por variavel com limite inferior positivo (`pool * p /\n" +
"  soma`, `soma >= 1`); o `lume certify` confere todos esses casos.\n" +
"- Recursao: a chamada recursiva precisa cumprir o `requires` da propria funcao (provado, ou refutado com\n" +
"  contraexemplo); o `lume certify` confere contrato recursivo por inducao, usando os contratos provados do\n" +
"  certificado nas chamadas que nao expande, e liga ao fonte (`--check-source`).\n" +
"- Booleanos nas provas: uma comparacao usada como valor (`= a + n <= 1000`, `ensures result == (a + n <= 1000)`,\n" +
"  `not f(n)`) e provada como 1 / 0. Uma law sobre uma chamada usa o `ensures` ja provado da funcao chamada quando a\n" +
"  hipotese da law implica o `requires` dela (vale para funcao que chama outras ou tem produto limitado).\n" +
"- Terminacao Composta e Kernel de Prova (`lcert.src`): Verifica obrigacoes compostas\n" +
"  `terminates` (`lk_prove_term_cond` com `and`/`or`) e executa autoteste criptografico\n" +
"  NIST FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 KAT (`sha256(\"abc\")`).\n\n" +
"## 4.3 Limite de Ciclos de Tempo Real (`@bound(cycles: N)`)\n" +
"Garante Worst-Case Execution Time (WCET) em kernels e drivers (`[V0002]`).\n\n" +
"## 4.4 Comandos de Prova e Autocura\n" +
"- `lume prove <arquivo.src>`           Prova todos os contratos e leis.\n" +
"- `lume verify [--jobs=N] <arquivo.src>...`  check, test, prove, fmt --check e certify em muitos arquivos; cache por arquivo.\n" +
"- `lume pkg publish|add|install`         versoes de pacotes: store com testes, requisitos `^`/`~`, lume_modules/, lume.lock.\n" +
"- `use std/hash|csv|utf8|datetime|regex|deflate|http|tls`  biblioteca padrao: hashes, CSV, UTF-8, datas e fusos, regex, gzip, HTTP e HTTPS.\n" +
"  Contratos dos builtins: `buf_bits_write` e `p + n` ou `-1`, `buf_get` 0..255, `buf_len` / `count` >= 0 (quando o\n" +
"  resultado tem nome num `let` ou e devolvido); limite no `requires` os operandos de uma clausula para ela nao estourar.\n" +
"- Exemplos oficiais: `examples/topics/*.src` (rode cada um com `lume test`) e `examples/diagnostics/` (por codigo, o\n" +
"  programa `.bad` que falha e o `.fixed.src` corrigido).\n" +
"- Um erro em tempo de execucao (exit 3) mostra a pilha depois da mensagem: `  at NOME (arquivo.src:LINHA)`, da mais interna para fora.\n" +
"- `lume certify <arquivo.src> --json`  Gera certificado criptografico de prova.\n" +
"- `lume heal <arquivo.src>`            Repara automaticamente contratos violados!\n" +
"- `lume equiv <spec.src> <rapido.src>` Prova que duas funcoes fazem a mesma coisa.\n" +
"- `lume agent cegis <arquivo.src>`     Sintetiza lacunas `??` usando CEGIS.\n"

fn man_pt_effects() = "# CAPITULO 5: EFEITOS ALGEBRICOS, MEMORIA DETERMINISTICA E ARENAS\n\n" +
"## 5.1 Efeitos Algebricos (`/ pure`, `/ " + man_br("io, fs, net") + "`)\n" +
"- Funcoes marcadas com `/ pure` sao matematicamente puras: nao podem acessar disco,\n" +
"  rede, processos ou mutar estado externo. Qualquer violacao gera `[E0200]`.\n" +
"- A lista de efeitos e opcional: sem `/ ...` os efeitos sao inferidos. Uma funcao que\n" +
"  declara a lista precisa nomear todos os efeitos que realiza, inclusive pelas funcoes\n" +
"  que chama; `[E0200]` diz quais faltam (`add '/ " + man_br("net, io") + "'`).\n" +
"- Efeitos dos builtins do runtime: `buf_*` (buffers de bytes mutaveis, alterados no\n" +
"  lugar) sao `io`, como todo builtin que le ou muda estado; `net_*` sao `net`; `fs_*`\n" +
"  sao `fs`. As funcoes de `use dns` sao `" + man_br("io, net, fs, time, panic") + "`. `f64` e os\n" +
"  builtins `f64_*` sao puros (sem efeito).\n\n" +
"## 5.2 Memoria Automatica, SRA Zero-Heap e Arenas (`std.arena`)\n" +
"A Lume recupera memoria sozinha: o runtime nativo tem um coletor mark-sweep nao movel que\n" +
"devolve memoria ao sistema. A pausa e proporcional ao heap vivo, nao ao lixo; um programa\n" +
"abaixo de 64 MiB nunca coleta. `own`, borrows e `resource type` sao regras de compilacao e nao\n" +
"dependem do coletor (`docs/38-memory-management.md`). Ele nao substitui as otimizacoes abaixo:\n" +
"reuso estatico Perceus onde a unicidade e provada + Escape Analysis / Scalar Replacement of\n" +
"Aggregates (`lsra_expr`: registros locais `let r = " + man_br("k1: v1, ...") + " in corpo` que nao escapam sao\n" +
"alocados diretamente em slots de pilha `%rbp` `_sra_<r>_<k>` com 0 alocacoes de heap) +\n" +
"palavras de valor (inteiro de 63 bits e string de ate 7 bytes dentro da palavra, sem heap; `int`\n" +
"continua com 64 bits) + tail-call `jmp` + arenas regionais `O(1)`:\n" +
"- `let a = arena_new(65536)`   Cria uma arena de 64 KB\n" +
"- `mem_pack(s)` / `mem_unpack(b)`   Comprime dados frios (formato de bloco LZ4; dado corrompido para)\n" +
"- `arena_freeze(a)` / `arena_thaw(a)`   Comprime uma arena; a pagina volta no primeiro toque\n" +
"- `arena_mark_secret(a)`, `@secret fn`   Segredos nunca chegam ao compactador ([C0009])\n" +
"- `arena_reset(a)` / `arena_destroy(a)`\n" +
"- `heap_stats()`               Retorna estatisticas do heap em tempo real\n" +
"- `gc_collect()` / `gc_count()` Forca uma coleta / conta as coletas\n" +
"- `lume run --memory <arq.src>` Mede o pico de memoria fisica (RSS em KB)\n" +
"- `LUME_HEAP_CAP=<bytes>`, `LUME_GC=on|off`, `LUME_GC_STRESS=<n>` Controlam o heap\n\n" +
"## 5.3 E-Capsules Reprodutiveis (`std.capsule`)\n" +
"- `lume capsule seal <arq.src> -o <saida.lcaps>` Sela codigo, entradas, saidas e SHA-256.\n" +
"- `lume capsule replay <saida.lcaps>`            Reproduz e audita a execucao selada.\n"

fn man_pt_stdlib() = "# CAPITULO 6: FUNCOES NATIVAS E BIBLIOTECA PADRAO DA LUME\n\n" +
"## 6.1 Funcoes Nativas (Sempre Disponiveis sem `use`)\n" +
"- Texto (`str`): `count(s)`, `at(s, i)`, `slice(s, ini, fim)`, `slicen(s, n, start, end)`,\n" +
"                 `ord(c)`, `chr(cod)`, `str(n)`, `toint(s)`\n" +
"- Arquivos (`fs`): `readall()`, `fs_read_file(caminho)`,\n" +
"                   `fs_write_sync(caminho, texto)`, `fs_path_exists(caminho)`,\n" +
"                   `fs_read_byte(caminho, offset)`\n" +
"                   `fs_read_range(caminho, offset, n)` (ate n bytes a partir do offset, sem ler o arquivo inteiro;\n" +
"                   menos no fim, \"\" depois dele), `fs_truncate(caminho, tamanho)` (1 / 0),\n" +
"                   `fs_rename_noreplace(de, para)` (0 quando `para` ja existe; nunca substitui)\n" +
"                   `fs_read_dir` segue link simbolico de pasta; no Windows `fs_chmod` com bits de grupo/outros faz o\n" +
"                   arquivo ou pasta privado voltar a herdar a ACL da pasta-mae\n" +
"- Arquivos so do dono (chaves, segredos): `fs_write_private(caminho, texto)` grava um temporario criado 0600\n" +
"                   (O_EXCL, sem seguir link), faz fsync e renomeia por cima: atomico, nunca legivel por outros,\n" +
"                   tambem no Windows (DACL protegida so com o dono); `fs_create_private(caminho, texto)` so cria\n" +
"                   se nao existe; `fs_mkdir_private(caminho)` cria pasta 0700 (uma existente e restringida);\n" +
"                   `fs_mode(caminho)` da os bits de permissao (384 = 0600, -1 se ilegivel; o Windows os compoe);\n" +
"                   `fs_is_private(caminho)` e 1 quando so o dono alcanca (recuse chave que outros leem, como o ssh)\n" +
"- Chaveiro do SO: `use keychain` -> `keychain_set(servico, conta, segredo)`, `keychain_get(servico, conta)`\n" +
"                   (" + man_br("ok, value, err") + "), `keychain_delete(servico, conta)`: Credential Manager no Windows; no Linux\n" +
"                   um arquivo so do dono, recusado na leitura se outros o alcancam; segredo de ate 2560 bytes\n" +
"                   `keychain_get_target(alvo)` le (so leitura) a credencial generica de outro programa pelo alvo exato\n" +
"                   (ex.: a do crate keyring do Rust): value (texto UTF-16LE) e raw (o blob)\n" +
"                   (com LUME_KEYCHAIN_DIR definido le esse diretorio; `keychain_set_target` grava so nele)\n" +
"                   Erros (`err`): `not_found` SO quando a entrada nao existe; `access_denied`, `unavailable` (sem\n" +
"                   cofre, sem sessao de logon, sem diretorio), `corrupt`, `not_private`, `locked` (reservado): um\n" +
"                   cofre que nao responde nunca vira ausente, o chamador pode falhar fechado\n" +
"- Ambiente: `os_getenv(nome)` (\"\" se ausente), `os_env_has(nome)` (1 se existe, mesmo vazia)\n" +
"- Interfaces virtuais (VPN): `use tun` -> `tun_open(nome)` -> {{ok, fd, sess, name, err}} (Linux /dev/net/tun como\n" +
"                   root; Windows Wintun em processo elevado, carregado so pelo camaleao (`chameleon_c_open`): caminho\n" +
"                   absoluto dentro de System32 ou Program Files com assinatura Authenticode valida (LUME_WINTUN_DLL,\n" +
"                   senao System32\\wintun.dll, depois Program Files\\WireGuard\\wintun.dll); a pasta do programa, a\n" +
"                   pasta atual, pastas de usuario e nome relativo sao recusados), `tun_read(t, buf)` (um pacote IP: o\n" +
"                   tamanho, 0 sem pacote, -1), `tun_write(t, buf,\n" +
"                   n)`, `tun_wait(t, ms)`, `tun_set_nonblocking(t)`, `tun_set_ipv4(t, end, prefixo)`, `tun_set_mtu(t, mtu)`,\n" +
"                   `tun_set_up(t)` (\"\" ou o motivo), `tun_close(t)`; no Linux o fd funciona com epoll\n" +
"- Controle de rede: `use netctl` -> `net_tcp_connect_addr_timeout(ip, porta, ms)` (o socket, ou -1 se recusado,\n" +
"                   inalcancavel ou calado alem de ms), `net_tcp_nodelay(fd, ligado)` (1 se aplicado); `use dns` ->\n" +
"                   `dns_tcp_connect_timeout(host, porta, ms)`. Escritos em Lume sobre as duas primitivas abaixo.\n" +
"                   Um laco atendendo muitos clientes: `net_set_nonblocking(fd, ligado)`, `net_send_some(fd, dados)`\n" +
"                   (bytes aceitos, 0 com o buffer cheio, -1 no erro; sem SIGPIPE), `net_recv_some(fd, max)` -> n > 0 /\n" +
"                   0 fechado / -2 nada agora / -1 erro, `epoll_add(ep, fd, tag, eventos)`, `epoll_mod`,\n" +
"                   `epoll_del(ep, fd)`, `epoll_wait_ev(ep, ms)` -> tag (-1 sem nada) e eventos (`epoll_in()`, `epoll_out()`)\n" +
"                   Connect sem travar o laco: `net_tcp_connect_start(ip, porta)` (fd na hora, connect em andamento;\n" +
"                   -1 no erro imediato), espere `epoll_out()`, depois `net_tcp_connect_result(fd)` -> 0 conectado,\n" +
"                   senao o numero do erro (111 recusado, 110 tempo esgotado)\n" +
"                   Enderecos: `net_local_addr(fd)`, `os_ipv4_interfaces()`, `os_ipv6_interfaces()` (forma curta, sem\n" +
"                   ::1, o de enlace local com o escopo: `fe80::1%3`), no Linux e no Windows\n" +
"- Primitivas de sistema (para runtime e bibliotecas, efeitos sys / io): `sys_call(nr, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5)` e a\n" +
"                   chamada ao sistema operacional (numeros do Linux, atendidos igual no Windows; ints pequenos;\n" +
"                   -errno na falha); `buf_addr(b)` e o endereco dos bytes de um buffer, para montar as estruturas\n" +
"- Sistema (`os`): `os_arg_count()`, `os_arg_at(i)`,\n" +
"                  `os_getpid()`, `os_exit(cod)`, `os_run(cmd, args)`,\n" +
"                  `os_run_capture_timeout(cmd, args, out, err, ms)`\n" +
"                  (o filho abre um grupo de processos novo; no prazo a arvore inteira e morta: kill(-pgid) no Linux,\n" +
"                  Job Object no Windows)\n" +
"                  `use process` -> `os_spawn_pipes(prog, args, novo_grupo)` (stdout e stderr em pipes),\n" +
"                  `os_fd_read_some(fd, max)` (n > 0, 0 fim, -2 nada agora, -1 erro; nunca bloqueia), `os_wait_nohang(pid)`,\n" +
"                  `os_wait_child(pid)`, `os_kill_tree(pid)`, `os_fd_close(fd)`,\n" +
"                  `os_run_capture_limit(prog, args, max_bytes, timeout_ms)` (no maximo max_bytes por stream, o resto\n" +
"                  drenado; arvore morta no prazo; status, exit_code, out, err, out_truncated, err_truncated, timed_out)\n" +
"- Inventario: `use sysinfo` -> `fs_statvfs(caminho)` (total, livre, disponivel, tipo), `net_interfaces()` (nome,\n" +
"                  MAC, up, enderecos com prefixo; sem loopback; Linux e Windows)\n" +
"- Sistema Windows (`use winsys`; no Linux tudo responde \"ausente\"): registro `reg_get_string(raiz, chave, nome)`,\n" +
"                  `reg_get_dword`, `reg_key_exists`, `reg_value_exists`; sessoes `wts_active_console_session()`,\n" +
"                  `wts_sessions()`, `wts_session_user(id)`, `process_session_id(pid)`; `services_running()`\n" +
"                  servicos: `svc_install`, `svc_start`, `svc_stop`, `svc_remove`, `svc_state`; como servico:\n" +
"                  `svc_dispatch_start`, `svc_next_event`, `svc_set_status`, `svc_finish`; sessao do usuario:\n" +
"                  `win_find_session_process`, `win_spawn_as_session`, `win_proc_alive`, `win_proc_exit_code`,\n" +
"                  `win_proc_terminate`, `win_handle_close`; named pipes: `pipe_server_create`, `pipe_server_accept`,\n" +
"                  `pipe_client_open`, `pipe_read_some`, `pipe_write_some`, `pipe_close` (sem bloqueio; com epoll);\n" +
"                  desktops: `win_input_desktop_open`, `win_desktop_name`, `win_set_thread_desktop`, `win_desktop_close`;\n" +
"                  janela de privacidade: `win_privacy_window_create`, `win_pump_messages`, `win_window_destroy`\n" +
"                  `fs_native_path(p)`: o caminho no formato do Windows (de /c/x para a forma com letra de unidade e\n" +
"                  barras invertidas); svc_install e win_spawn_as_session ja convertem o executavel\n" +
"                  tela, captura e entrada (agentes e visualizadores de acesso remoto; o processo passa a Per-Monitor-V2):\n" +
"                  `win_displays()` (indice, nome, x, y, largura, altura, dpi, escala, rotacao, primario, frequencia,\n" +
"                  monitor), `win_virtual_screen()`; `win_capture_open(indice)` (Desktop Duplication via Direct3D 11,\n" +
"                  GDI BitBlt quando nao houver: modo \"dxgi\" / \"gdi\"), `win_capture_frame(cap, timeout_ms)` e\n" +
"                  `win_capture_frame_into(cap, timeout_ms, buf)` -> status \"frame\" (BGRA, stride, retangulos sujos),\n" +
"                  \"pointer\", \"timeout\", \"lost\" (reabrir: troca de desktop, UAC, tela de bloqueio) ou \"error\", com a\n" +
"                  posicao do ponteiro; `win_capture_close`, `win_capture_gdi(x, y, w, h)`; `win_cursor()`,\n" +
"                  `win_cursor_shape(handle)` (largura, altura, hot_x, hot_y, cor e mascara BGRA, mono)\n" +
"                  entrada: `win_send_key(scancode, estendida, desce)` (Set 1), `win_send_vk(vk, desce)`,\n" +
"                  `win_send_text(s)` (Unicode), `win_send_mouse_move(x, y)` (absoluto no desktop virtual),\n" +
"                  `win_send_mouse_button(botao, desce)`, `win_send_mouse_wheel(delta, horizontal)` (1/120),\n" +
"                  `win_key_state(vk)`, `win_async_key_down(vk)`, `win_send_sas(como_usuario)` (Ctrl+Alt+Del)\n" +
"                  janela do visualizador (sem callback: o programa bombeia): `win_window_open(titulo, w, h)`,\n" +
"                  `win_window_events(hwnd)`, `win_window_alive`, `win_window_client_size`, `win_window_set_title`,\n" +
"                  `win_window_draw(hwnd, dados, w, h, stride)`, `win_window_draw_rect`; gancho WH_KEYBOARD_LL:\n" +
"                  `win_kbhook_install()`, `win_kbhook_swallow(hwnd, liga)`, `win_kbhook_events()`, `win_kbhook_remove`\n" +
"- Buffers de bytes (mutaveis): `buf_new(n)`, `buf_len(b)`, `buf_get(b, i)` (0..255), `buf_set(b, i, v)` (devolve b),\n" +
"                  `buf_copy(dst, d_off, src, s_off, n)`, `buf_slice(b, off, n)`, `buf_from_str(s)`, `buf_to_str(b, off,\n" +
"                  n)`, `buf_addr(b)`; buf_get / buf_set com indice pequeno viram codigo de maquina inline (sem chamada)\n" +
"                  video: `buf_bgra_to_i420(src, stride, w, h, dst)` e `buf_i420_to_bgra(src, w, h, dst, stride)` (BT.601\n" +
"                  faixa limitada, media 2x2 do croma, tamanhos impares; bytes escritos ou -1; quadro 1080p em poucos ms)\n" +
"                  distorcao de bloco para codificadores: `buf_sad16x16`, `buf_sad8x8`, `buf_sad4x4`, `buf_satd4x4`,\n" +
"                  `buf_satd16x16` (a, ai, sa, b, bi, sb): soma das diferencas absolutas, ou da diferenca transformada\n" +
"                  por Hadamard 4x4 / 2, entre o bloco n x n de a no byte ai (linhas a sa bytes) e o de b em bi; -1 se errado\n" +
"                  blocos H.264: `buf_h264_fdct4x4` / `idct4x4(src, si, dst, di)` (int16 4x4), `buf_h264_quant4x4(src,\n" +
"                  si, qp, intra, dst, di)` (niveis nao nulos), `buf_h264_dequant4x4(src, si, qp, dst, di)`,\n" +
"                  `buf_h264_sub4x4(a, ai, sa, pred, pi, dst)`, `buf_h264_recon4x4(pred, pi, res, ri, dst, di)`,\n" +
"                  `buf_h264_intra4x4` / `intra16x16(frame, fi, fs, modo, disp, dst)`; com `use h264`:\n" +
"                  `buf_h264_luma_mc(ref, ri, rs, rw, rh, x, y, mx, my, w, h, dst, di, ds)` (1/4 de amostra, 6 taps),\n" +
"                  `buf_h264_chroma_mc` (mesmos argumentos, 1/8, bilinear), `buf_h264_deblock_edge(buf, q0, across,\n" +
"                  along, lines, bs, alpha, beta, tc0, chroma)` (bs, tc0: listas, um valor por 4 linhas de luma / 2 de\n" +
"                  croma); todos devolvem -1 com argumento errado\n" +
"                  escrita de bits (codificadores de entropia, bit mais significativo primeiro): `buf_bits_write(b,\n" +
"                  pos, v, n)` (os n bits baixos de v, 1..32, no bit pos; devolve pos + n), `buf_bits_read(b, pos, n)`,\n" +
"                  `buf_bits_ue(b, pos, v)` / `buf_bits_se(b, pos, v)` (Exp-Golomb, devolvem a nova pos); -1 se errado\n" +
"- Hardware, Kernel Bare-Metal e Console Nativo (`@freestanding` / `.kernel` / `.iso`):\n" +
"  - Portas I/O (8/16/32 bits): `port_out8(p, v)`, `port_in8(p)`, `port_out16(p, v)`, `port_in16(p)`,\n" +
"                               `port_out32(p, v)`, `port_in32(p)`\n" +
"  - MMIO Volatil (8/16/32/64 bits): `mmio_volatile_write8(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read8(a)`,\n" +
"                                    `mmio_volatile_write16(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read16(a)`,\n" +
"                                    `mmio_volatile_write32(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read32(a)`,\n" +
"                                    `mmio_volatile_write64(a, v)`, `mmio_volatile_read64(a)`\n" +
"  - Console VGA Nativo (`0xB8000` + CRT `0x3D4`/`0x3D5`): `vga_puts(row, col, attr, texto)`,\n" +
"    `vga_fill_row(row, attr, ch_ascii)`, `vga_scroll_up(top_row, bot_row, attr)`,\n" +
"    `vga_set_cursor(row, col)`\n" +
"  - CPU, MSR e SMP: `cpu_cli()`, `cpu_sti()`, `cpu_hlt()`, `cpu_pause()`, `cpu_mfence()`,\n" +
"                    `cpu_rdtsc()`, `cpu_rdmsr(msr)`, `cpu_wrmsr(msr, val)`, `cpu_read_cr3()`,\n" +
"                    `cpu_write_cr3(v)`, `cpu_invlpg(va)`, `cpu_idt_init()`, `cpu_smp_boot_ap(v)`\n" +
"  - Bitwise de 64 bits em Hardware: `bit_and(a, b)`, `bit_or(a, b)`, `bit_xor(a, b)`,\n" +
"                                    `bit_not(a)`, `bit_shl(a, n)`, `bit_shr(a, n)`\n" +
"  - Intrinsecos Constant-Time: `ct_select(mask, a, b)` (bit a bit: `a` onde o bit da mascara esta ligado, senao `b`),\n" +
"                               `ct_eq(a, b)` (1 se iguais, senao 0); sem desvio em um kernel constant-time\n" +
"  - Bloco de Memoria, Integridade e Estado O(1): `mem_copy(dst, src, len)`, `mem_set(dst, b, len)`,\n" +
"    `mem_crc64(addr, len)` (auditoria anti-rootkit FNV-1a de 64 bits), `krn_slot_write(idx, val)`,\n" +
"    `krn_slot_read(idx)` (tabela de estado de kernel de 1024 slots com zero alocacoes de heap)\n" +
"- Falha Segura:   `ctfail(msg)` (imprime erro no `stderr` e encerra com codigo != 0)\n\n" +
"## 6.2 Modulos da Biblioteca Padrao (`use <modulo>`)\n" +
"- Modulos: `use json as j` e depois `j.read(s)` (sempre a funcao do modulo, mesmo com uma variavel local\n" +
"  `read`); um modulo numa pasta e escrito pelo ultimo segmento (`use\n" +
"  net/http` -> `http.get(u)`); de duas pastas com o mesmo ultimo segmento, todas menos uma precisam de alias\n" +
"  (`use a/http` + `use b/http as hb`), e duas sem alias param em `arquivo:linha:coluna` com a correcao; cada\n" +
"  `use m` e resolvido ao lado do arquivo que o escreve; nomes repetidos ficam separados (NOME__modulo)\n" +
"- `use seq`            Repeticao sem recursao escrita a mao: `seq_map`, `seq_filter`, `seq_fold`, `seq_foldr`,\n" +
"                       `seq_any`, `seq_all`, `seq_find`, `seq_range`, `seq_loop(a, b, acc, f)`, `seq_while(estado, cond, passo)`,\n" +
"                       `seq_count`, `seq_bytes`, `seq_loop_inv(a, b, acc, passo, inv)` (`lume prove` prova o contrato por\n" +
"                       inducao no invariante); recursao de cauda, um milhao de passos em pilha constante; lambdas\n" +
"                       `fn(x) => ...` capturam variaveis. Lacos: `seq_loop(0, n, acc0, fn(i, acc) => ...)` e o `for i in 0..n`\n" +
"                       sobre um acumulador, sem montar lista: `fn soma_buf(b) = seq_loop(0, buf_len(b), 0, fn(i, acc) => acc +\n" +
"                       buf_get(b, i))`; `seq_loop_down(a, b, acc, f)` conta para baixo, `seq_while(s, cond, passo)` repete enquanto cond(s)\n" +
"- `use text`           Achar por conteudo, nao por coluna: `str_find(s, sub, desde)` (indice ou -1),\n" +
"                       `str_find_last`, `str_contains`, `str_after(s, rotulo)`, `str_before`, `str_between`,\n" +
"                       `str_trim`, `str_lines` / `str_line(s, n)` (so \"\\n\" quebra linha, como sed e awk),\n" +
"                       `str_line_with`, `str_hex_tokens(s)` (palavras hex, sem 0x, `00 10` / `00:10` unidos),\n" +
"                       `str_hex_after(linha, \"quic key:\")` para vetores de teste lidos do texto de RFCs\n" +
"- Profundidade de recursao: o runtime reserva uma pilha grande ao iniciar (Linux e Windows): recursao comum\n" +
"                       de um milhao de niveis roda, dezenas de milhoes de quadros pequenos tambem; alem disso o programa\n" +
"                       para com `lume: stack overflow (recursion too deep)` (saida 12), nunca em silencio\n" +
